{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_32","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command '$n=0; Get-Content -LiteralPath '\"'docs/HANDOFF_LOG.md' | ForEach-Object { \"'$n++; if($n -ge 1 -and $n -le 100) { '\"'{0,5}: {1}' -f \"'$n,$_ } }'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command '$n=0; Get-Content -LiteralPath '\"'nodes/_otr_video_engines/frame_contract.py' | ForEach-Object { \"'$n++; if($n -ge 1 -and $n -le 240) { '\"'{0,5}: {1}' -f \"'$n,$_ } }'","aggregated_output":"    1: \"\"\"THE DECLARATION SURFACE: what an adapter can render, and how it joins.\r\n    2: \r\n    3: Multi-clip beat coverage (2026-07-25, chunk 2). The operator's requirement is\r\n    4: that a beat be covered by enough REAL rendered clips to be moving video, with\r\n    5: chaining preferred and a jump cut acceptable. That is only decidable if each\r\n    6: adapter DECLARES two things the partitioner can reason about without ever\r\n    7: loading a model:\r\n    8: \r\n    9: * :class:`FrameContract` -- the legal render lengths. Pure, STATIC numbers:\r\n   10:   never live VRAM, never mutable environment. Stills are minted before the\r\n   11:   render phase, so a partition computed from runtime state would be a partition\r\n   12:   the image phase could not have planned for.\r\n   13: * :data:`CONTINUITY_MODES` -- whether segment N+1 can actually begin on segment\r\n   14:   N's terminal frame. \"Accepts a still\" is NOT \"guarantees first-frame\r\n   15:   continuity\": ``accepts_still`` only controls minting (``motion_common.py:393``),\r\n   16:   HuMo's reference is a soft identity hint per the Bug Bible, and Veo's\r\n   17:   ``lastFrame`` is first/last INTERPOLATION inside ONE clip, not chaining.\r\n   18:   Engines without strict first-frame support get a JUMP CUT, which is legal and\r\n   19:   honest; silently pretending they chain is neither.\r\n   20: \r\n   21: EVERY ENGINE GETS THE SAME TERMS (chunk 7a, 2026-07-26). This module used to\r\n   22: open with \"EVERY ADAPTER IS ``single_only`` UNTIL IT PROVES OTHERWISE\" and\r\n   23: carried a ``supports_multi_clip`` flag that each adapter had to set for itself.\r\n   24: The operator ended that design: \"this architecture should work with all video\r\n   25: and still models. There's no gate with opt in or opt out. If there is, we need\r\n   26: to remove that. Everything gets an equal term... I don't like any hidden\r\n   27: opt-ins. It either works or it fails.\"\r\n   28: \r\n   29: So the flag is gone and multi-clip is universal. What an adapter must still\r\n   30: EARN, per engine and from evidence, is the CHAIN -- see :data:`CONTINUITY_MODES`\r\n   31: below. An engine that cannot prove first-frame lock gets an honest jump cut,\r\n   32: which is legal; it does not get a pretended seam.\r\n   33: \r\n   34: :data:`SINGLE_ONLY` survives as the resolution for an engine that declares\r\n   35: NOTHING, and ``tests/test_engine_contract_roster.py`` fails by name if any\r\n   36: registered engine ever resolves to it again.\r\n   37: \r\n   38: Cold-import clean: stdlib only, no registry import at module scope.\r\n   39: \"\"\"\r\n   40: \r\n   41: from __future__ import annotations\r\n   42: \r\n   43: from dataclasses import dataclass, field, replace\r\n   44: \r\n   45: \r\n   46: #: Segment N+1 starts EXACTLY on segment N's terminal frame; the adapter\r\n   47: #: guarantees first-frame lock. Only this earns a CHAIN.\r\n   48: CONTINUITY_STRICT_FIRST_FRAME = \"strict_first_frame\"\r\n   49: \r\n   50: #: The adapter accepts a reference image but does not guarantee it as frame 0\r\n   51: #: (HuMo's identity hint, Veo's interpolation endpoints). NOT chainable --\r\n   52: #: these take a jump cut.\r\n   53: CONTINUITY_SOFT_REFERENCE = \"soft_reference\"\r\n   54: \r\n   55: #: No continuity mechanism at all (procedural visualizers, text-to-video).\r\n   56: CONTINUITY_NONE = \"none\"\r\n   57: \r\n   58: CONTINUITY_MODES = (\r\n   59:     CONTINUITY_STRICT_FIRST_FRAME,\r\n   60:     CONTINUITY_SOFT_REFERENCE,\r\n   61:     CONTINUITY_NONE,\r\n   62: )\r\n   63: \r\n   64: \r\n   65: class FrameContractError(ValueError):\r\n   66:     \"\"\"An adapter declared a frame contract that cannot be satisfied.\"\"\"\r\n   67: \r\n   68: \r\n   69: class ContractEnvConflict(RuntimeError):\r\n   70:     \"\"\"The ENVIRONMENT asked for something a static declaration forbids.\r\n   71: \r\n   72:     Deliberately NOT a :class:`FrameContractError`. That one means \"the\r\n   73:     declaration itself is incoherent\" and is raised at construction, so it can\r\n   74:     never reach a render. This one means \"the declaration is fine and the box\r\n   75:     was told something else\", which is a runtime condition an operator caused\r\n   76:     and an operator can fix -- so it carries the variable name and the legal\r\n   77:     values, and is caught by nothing.\r\n   78: \r\n   79:     SCOPE, HONESTLY (2026-07-26). Only ``word_razzle`` raises this today, for\r\n   80:     an env duration outside its provider's fixed menu. The wider question --\r\n   81:     whether an env var may lower a declared CEILING at all -- is deliberately\r\n   82:     NOT answered here: several of those vars are documented operator knobs for\r\n   83:     VRAM-constrained boxes (the WAN 8GB launch contract depends on one), so\r\n   84:     refusing them outright would break a real production path. The fork is\r\n   85:     written up in ``docs/2026-07-26-chunk-7b-window-prompt.md`` under OPEN\r\n   86:     DECISION and is the operator's to settle.\r\n   87:     \"\"\"\r\n   88: \r\n   89: \r\n   90: @dataclass(frozen=True)\r\n   91: class FrameContract:\r\n   92:     \"\"\"The STATIC, PURE set of render lengths an adapter will accept.\r\n   93: \r\n   94:     ``min_frames`` / ``max_frames``\r\n   95:         Inclusive bounds on ONE render call. ``max_frames`` is the adapter's\r\n   96:         own hard ceiling, not a VRAM guess.\r\n   97:     ``quantum``\r\n   98:         Legal lengths are ``min_frames + k * quantum``. An ``8n+1`` engine\r\n   99:         declares ``min_frames=9, quantum=8``. ``1`` means any length in range.\r\n  100:     ``discrete_frames``\r\n  101:         For providers that only accept a fixed menu of clip lengths (Veo's\r\n  102:         4/6/8 SECONDS). When non-empty this REPLACES the min/max/quantum\r\n  103:         arithmetic and the legal lengths are exactly these values.\r\n  104: \r\n  105:         THE UNIT IS FRAMES, NOT SECONDS. ``coverage_plan`` compares these\r\n  106:         numbers against ``target_visible_frames`` directly, so a provider menu\r\n  107:         expressed in seconds MUST be multiplied by :attr:`native_fps` at the\r\n  108:         declaration site. Veo's 4/6/8 s at 24 fps declares ``(96, 144, 192)``.\r\n  109:         The field was named ``discrete_durations`` until 2026-07-26; it was\r\n  110:         renamed because the old name invited exactly that seconds-for-frames\r\n  111:         substitution, and a validator cannot catch it -- ``(4, 6, 8)`` is a\r\n  112:         perfectly well-formed frame menu, just a wrong one.\r\n  113:     ``native_fps``\r\n  114:         The frame rate these frame numbers are expressed at, or ``0`` for an\r\n  115:         engine that renders at whatever the canvas asks for. Static and\r\n  116:         informational: it is what lets the matrix report seconds, and what\r\n  117:         tells a reader that a 24 fps provider is being planned against a\r\n  118:         25 fps canvas. It is NOT read by the partitioner.\r\n  119:     ``allow_tail_trim``\r\n  120:         Whether the assembler may render the smallest covering length and trim\r\n  121:         the excess at canonicalization. Discrete-duration lanes REQUIRE this --\r\n  122:         4/6/8s durations cannot sum to an arbitrary beat.\r\n  123:     ``continuity``\r\n  124:         One of :data:`CONTINUITY_MODES`.\r\n  125: \r\n  126:     Frozen, so a contract cannot be mutated after an adapter publishes it --\r\n  127:     the partitioner and the image phase must read the same numbers.\r\n  128:     \"\"\"\r\n  129: \r\n  130:     min_frames: int = 1\r\n  131:     max_frames: int = 0            # 0 == \"unbounded / not declared\"\r\n  132:     quantum: int = 1\r\n  133:     discrete_frames: tuple = field(default_factory=tuple)\r\n  134:     native_fps: int = 0            # 0 == \"renders at the canvas rate\"\r\n  135:     allow_tail_trim: bool = False\r\n  136:     continuity: str = CONTINUITY_NONE\r\n  137: \r\n  138:     def __post_init__(self):\r\n  139:         if self.continuity not in CONTINUITY_MODES:\r\n  140:             raise FrameContractError(\r\n  141:                 \"continuity %r is not one of %r\" % (self.continuity,\r\n  142:                                                     CONTINUITY_MODES))\r\n  143:         if int(self.min_frames) < 1:\r\n  144:             raise FrameContractError(\r\n  145:                 \"min_frames must be >= 1, got %r\" % (self.min_frames,))\r\n  146:         if int(self.quantum) < 1:\r\n  147:             raise FrameContractError(\r\n  148:                 \"quantum must be >= 1, got %r\" % (self.quantum,))\r\n  149:         if self.max_frames and int(self.max_frames) < int(self.min_frames):\r\n  150:             raise FrameContractError(\r\n  151:                 \"max_frames %r is below min_frames %r\"\r\n  152:                 % (self.max_frames, self.min_frames))\r\n  153:         if int(self.native_fps) < 0:\r\n  154:             raise FrameContractError(\r\n  155:                 \"native_fps must be >= 0, got %r\" % (self.native_fps,))\r\n  156:         if self.discrete_frames:\r\n  157:             if any(int(d) < 1 for d in self.discrete_frames):\r\n  158:                 raise FrameContractError(\r\n  159:                     \"discrete_frames must all be >= 1, got %r\"\r\n  160:                     % (self.discrete_frames,))\r\n  161:             if not self.allow_tail_trim:\r\n  162:                 # A fixed menu of lengths cannot sum to an arbitrary beat, so\r\n  163:                 # without tail trimming there are beats this engine could never\r\n  164:                 # cover exactly -- that is a contract that lies.\r\n  165:                 raise FrameContractError(\r\n  166:                     \"discrete_frames requires allow_tail_trim=True: a fixed \"\r\n  167:                     \"length menu cannot sum to an arbitrary beat length\")\r\n  168: \r\n  169:     # -- pure queries -------------------------------------------------- #\r\n  170: \r\n  171:     def is_legal_length(self, n: int) -> bool:\r\n  172:         \"\"\"True iff ``n`` is a length this adapter will accept in one call.\"\"\"\r\n  173:         n = int(n)\r\n  174:         if self.discrete_frames:\r\n  175:             return n in tuple(int(d) for d in self.discrete_frames)\r\n  176:         if n < int(self.min_frames):\r\n  177:             return False\r\n  178:         if self.max_frames and n > int(self.max_frames):\r\n  179:             return False\r\n  180:         return (n - int(self.min_frames)) % int(self.quantum) == 0\r\n  181: \r\n  182:     def legal_lengths(self) -> tuple:\r\n  183:         \"\"\"Every legal length, ascending. Empty when unbounded (nothing to\r\n  184:         enumerate -- callers must use :meth:`is_legal_length` instead).\"\"\"\r\n  185:         if self.discrete_frames:\r\n  186:             return tuple(sorted(int(d) for d in self.discrete_frames))\r\n  187:         if not self.max_frames:\r\n  188:             return ()\r\n  189:         return tuple(range(int(self.min_frames), int(self.max_frames) + 1,\r\n  190:                            int(self.quantum)))\r\n  191: \r\n  192:     def largest_legal_at_most(self, n: int):\r\n  193:         \"\"\"The largest legal length <= ``n``, or None if there is none.\"\"\"\r\n  194:         n = int(n)\r\n  195:         if self.discrete_frames:\r\n  196:             fits = [int(d) for d in self.discrete_frames if int(d) <= n]\r\n  197:             return max(fits) if fits else None\r\n  198:         if n < int(self.min_frames):\r\n  199:             return None\r\n  200:         capped = min(n, int(self.max_frames)) if self.max_frames else n\r\n  201:         steps = (capped - int(self.min_frames)) // int(self.quantum)\r\n  202:         return int(self.min_frames) + steps * int(self.quantum)\r\n  203: \r\n  204:     def smallest_legal_at_least(self, n: int):\r\n  205:         \"\"\"The smallest legal length >= ``n``, or None if it exceeds the\r\n  206:         ceiling. Used with ``allow_tail_trim`` to cover a remainder exactly.\"\"\"\r\n  207:         n = max(int(n), int(self.min_frames))\r\n  208:         if self.discrete_frames:\r\n  209:             fits = [int(d) for d in self.discrete_frames if int(d) >= n]\r\n  210:             return min(fits) if fits else None\r\n  211:         steps = -(-(n - int(self.min_frames)) // int(self.quantum))  # ceil div\r\n  212:         candidate = int(self.min_frames) + steps * int(self.quantum)\r\n  213:         if self.max_frames and candidate > int(self.max_frames):\r\n  214:             return None\r\n  215:         return candidate\r\n  216: \r\n  217: \r\n  218: #: What an engine that declares NOTHING resolves to: unbounded, quantum 1, no\r\n  219: #: chaining. Every length is legal, so it never splits and never refuses -- the\r\n  220: #: pre-7a behaviour of the whole tree, kept as the honest answer for a stub, a\r\n  221: #: custom slot, or an adapter that failed to import. No REGISTERED engine may\r\n  222: #: resolve to it; ``tests/test_engine_contract_roster.py`` fails by name if one\r\n  223: #: does.\r\n  224: SINGLE_ONLY = FrameContract()\r\n  225: \r\n  226: \r\n  227: def frame_contract_for(engine) -> FrameContract:\r\n  228:     \"\"\"Resolve one adapter's declared contract, defaulting to SINGLE_ONLY.\r\n  229: \r\n  230:     Accepts either a ``frame_contract()`` method or a ``frame_contract``\r\n  231:     attribute, matching how the rest of the adapter surface duck-types. An\r\n  232:     adapter that declares nothing, or whose declaration raises, is treated as\r\n  233:     ``single_only`` -- the safe direction, because the worst case is that a\r\n  234:     beat renders exactly the way it does today.\r\n  235:     \"\"\"\r\n  236:     if engine is None:\r\n  237:         return SINGLE_ONLY\r\n  238:     declared = getattr(engine, \"frame_contract\", None)\r\n  239:     if declared is None:\r\n  240:         return SINGLE_ONLY\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command '$n=0; Get-Content -LiteralPath '\"'nodes/_otr_video_engines/eng_wan_ti2v.py' | ForEach-Object { \"'$n++; if($n -ge 1 -and $n -le 320) { '\"'{0,5}: {1}' -f \"'$n,$_ } }'","aggregated_output":"    1: \"\"\"Wan 2.2 TI2V-5B image->video motion adapter (8GB tier) -- in-process, default-OFF.\r\n    2: \r\n    3: The 5B TI2V sibling of ``wan_i2v``. It animates a still into motion on the 5B\r\n    4: Wan 2.2 model, which the distribution targets at the 8GB tier (GGUF Q5_K_M ~3.6 GB\r\n    5: UNET; Apache-2.0, commercial-clean). It runs on CORE ComfyUI Wan nodes -- NOT the\r\n    6: KJ wrapper (same BUG-070 / numpy-pin reasons as wan_i2v).\r\n    7: \r\n    8: The 5B graph DIFFERS from the 14B I2V graph: the 5B uses ``Wan22ImageToVideoLatent``\r\n    9: (vae/width/height/length/batch_size + optional start_image -> LATENT) rather than\r\n   10: ``WanImageToVideo`` (which bundles positive/negative/latent), so the KSampler takes\r\n   11: the CLIPTextEncode positive/negative DIRECTLY and the latent from\r\n   12: ``Wan22ImageToVideoLatent``. The 5B core node class + the loader presence were\r\n   13: captured from a LIVE ``/object_info`` on the 5080 (2026-06-14, VERIFY-AT-BUILD,\r\n   14: GO_FORWARD 4A) before this engine was coded.\r\n   15: \r\n   16: The 5B REQUIRES the Wan2.2 VAE (``wan2.2_vae.safetensors``) -- its latent\r\n   17: compression differs from the 2.1 VAE, so feeding the 2.1 VAE corrupts the decode.\r\n   18: ``assert_usable`` fails CLOSED (M8) if the resolved VAE basename is empty or is the\r\n   19: 2.1 VAE. The umt5 CLIP is shared with wan_i2v.\r\n   20: \r\n   21: Registered DEFAULT-OFF / dark (empty ``default_roles`` + gated behind\r\n   22: ``OTR_ENABLE_WAN_TI2V``); fails CLOSED until the operator enables it AND the GGUF +\r\n   23: the Wan2.2 VAE are on disk. The pure dims/aspect/materialize/canonicalize helpers +\r\n   24: the M7 silent-clip contract proof are SHARED with wan_i2v via :mod:`wan_shared`;\r\n   25: the loaders, node candidates and the 5B graph below are engine-specific. Import-time\r\n   26: is cold-import clean (V-12). UTF-8, no BOM, ASCII-only.\r\n   27: \r\n   28: Config (env). READ THE SPLIT -- since the WAN recipe freeze (2026-07-27) the\r\n   29: render knobs do NOT bind on a production leg:\r\n   30: \r\n   31: * STILL LIVE, every leg -- ASSET LOCATION and the render-length CEILING, never\r\n   32:   the recipe: ``OTR_ENABLE_WAN_TI2V`` (vestigial opt-in flag);\r\n   33:   ``OTR_WAN_TI2V_CKPT`` the GGUF (or safetensors) UNET path the load probe\r\n   34:   checks; ``OTR_WAN_TI2V_UNET_NAME`` / ``OTR_WAN_TI2V_CLIP_NAME`` /\r\n   35:   ``OTR_WAN_TI2V_VAE_NAME`` loader basenames; ``OTR_WAN_TI2V_LOADER`` /\r\n   36:   ``OTR_WAN_TI2V_CLIP_LOADER`` gguf|safetensors (else INFERRED from the\r\n   37:   resolved basename -- they stay live WITH the names they follow, because\r\n   38:   freezing the loader class while its filename still moved would give one fact\r\n   39:   two owners); ``OTR_WAN_TI2V_CLIP_DIR`` / ``OTR_WAN_TI2V_VAE_DIR`` /\r\n   40:   ``OTR_WAN_TI2V_UNET_DIR`` dir overrides; and ``OTR_WAN_TI2V_MAX_FRAMES``,\r\n   41:   which is a CEILING rather than a recipe value and is the shipped 8GB tier's\r\n   42:   ``launch.env`` channel (``config/profiles/otr_8gb_wan.json``).\r\n   43: * FROZEN IN CODE as ``WAN_TI2V_RECIPE``, ignored-with-a-warning:\r\n   44:   ``OTR_WAN_TI2V_STEPS`` / ``_CFG`` / ``_SHIFT`` / ``_SAMPLER`` / ``_SCHEDULER``\r\n   45:   / ``_NEGATIVE`` / ``_TILED_VAE`` / ``_VAE_TILE`` / ``_VAE_OVERLAP`` /\r\n   46:   ``_VAE_TEMPORAL`` / ``_VAE_TEMPORAL_OVERLAP``. Their defaults live in that\r\n   47:   dict, not here, so this list cannot drift from the values.\r\n   48: * THE CONSENT ACT: set ``OTR_WAN_TI2V_PREQUALIFICATION=1`` and the frozen knobs\r\n   49:   bind again, range-checked and fail-closed, for a MEASUREMENT run -- whose\r\n   50:   clips stamp a ``+prequalification`` recipe receipt so a sweep artifact is\r\n   51:   never mistaken for a production one.\r\n   52: \r\n   53: Why the freeze: a production episode is submitted to an ALREADY-BOOTED server,\r\n   54: so a knob exported at launch cannot bind the work (``PBUG-20260723-02``). Code\r\n   55: binds on every leg; an environment cannot.\r\n   56: \"\"\"\r\n   57: from __future__ import annotations\r\n   58: \r\n   59: import logging\r\n   60: import os\r\n   61: \r\n   62: from . import motion_common as _MC\r\n   63: from . import recipe_departures as _RD\r\n   64: from . import wan_recipe as _WR\r\n   65: from . import wan_shared as _WS\r\n   66: from .._otr_shared.role_compat import ROLES\r\n   67: from .._otr_shared.still_plan_helpers import StillPlanRow\r\n   68: from .frame_contract import CONTINUITY_STRICT_FIRST_FRAME, FrameContract\r\n   69: from .registry import EngineUnusable, EngineUsabilityReason, register\r\n   70: from .wan_shared import (\r\n   71:     _WAN_DEFAULT_NEGATIVE, ffprobe_clip_fields, validate_silent_clip_contract)\r\n   72: \r\n   73: _LOG = logging.getLogger(\"OTR.video.wan_ti2v\")\r\n   74: \r\n   75: _THIS = os.path.abspath(__file__)\r\n   76: _REPO_ROOT = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(_THIS)))\r\n   77: _COMFY_ROOT = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(_REPO_ROOT))\r\n   78: \r\n   79: #: The 2.1 VAE basename the 5B must NOT use (M8): its latent compression differs.\r\n   80: _WAN21_VAE_BASENAME = \"wan_2.1_vae.safetensors\"\r\n   81: #: The APPROVED Wan2.2 VAE basenames (floor fail-closed whitelist, 2026-06-18\r\n   82: #: roundtable): any other present-but-wrong VAE corrupts the 5B decode, so the\r\n   83: #: guard accepts only these rather than merely rejecting empty / the 2.1 VAE.\r\n   84: _WAN22_VAE_ALLOWED = frozenset({\"wan2.2_vae.safetensors\"})\r\n   85: #: Default 8GB-tier GGUF (Q5_K_M; Apache-2.0). Resolved via folder_paths /\r\n   86: #: OTR_WAN_TI2V_CKPT at runtime; this basename is the fallback the loader reads.\r\n   87: _TI2V_DEFAULT_UNET = \"Wan2.2-TI2V-5B-Q5_K_M.gguf\"\r\n   88: #: Floor default umt5 CLIP = the GGUF encoder (2026-06-18 roundtable). The official\r\n   89: #: fp8 (umt5_xxl_fp8_e4m3fn_scaled.safetensors) throws Float8_e4m3fn on Mac MPS\r\n   90: #: (ComfyUI #9255); GGUF dequantizes to fp16 -> the cross-platform 8GB path. Override\r\n   91: #: with OTR_WAN_TI2V_CLIP_NAME (+ OTR_WAN_TI2V_CLIP_LOADER) for an fp16 safetensors.\r\n   92: _TI2V_DEFAULT_CLIP = \"umt5-xxl-encoder-Q5_K_M.gguf\"\r\n   93: # Frame budgeting (2026-06-18 CLIP-FILL roundtable, supersedes the static 8GB\r\n   94: # floor): the old code hard-CLAMPED every clip to 17 frames (0.68s @ 25fps) so a\r\n   95: # ~280-frame beat froze after 0.68s (the composite held the last frame). The fix\r\n   96: # PREDICTS the VRAM-affordable length per beat via motion_common.\r\n   97: # compute_real_frame_budget (a zero-cost mem_get_info read + a cost model -- never\r\n   98: # react-to-OOM) bounded by the beat's audio-derived target, then the render\r\n   99: # ping-pong-extends that short render up to the full target so the beat is FILLED\r\n  100: # with motion. _TI2V_MIN_FRAMES is the motion floor (always >= this many 4n+1\r\n  101: # frames of real motion); _TI2V_MAX_FRAMES is the absolute hard cap;\r\n  102: # OTR_WAN_TI2V_MAX_FRAMES (server boot env) or the tier profile's\r\n  103: # video.max_render_frames (ledger-stamped, the production channel) lets a\r\n  104: # tiny/8GB card pin a lower hard cap.\r\n  105: _TI2V_MIN_FRAMES = 17\r\n  106: _TI2V_DEFAULT_FRAMES = 17\r\n  107: _TI2V_MAX_FRAMES = 177\r\n  108: #: Reference render canvas used when _floor_length is called without explicit dims\r\n  109: #: (matches OTR_VIDEO_LANDSCAPE_CANVAS / the cost-model telemetry reference).\r\n  110: _TI2V_COST_REF_W = 1472\r\n  111: _TI2V_COST_REF_H = 832\r\n  112: \r\n  113: #: The defined recipe-receipt string threaded into the manifest.\r\n  114: #:\r\n  115: #: THE VERSION LIVES IN THE STRING, not in a separate constant. This value rides\r\n  116: #: ``_clip_from_raw`` -> the manifest row -> the render-batch receipt ->\r\n  117: #: ``stamp_durable(meta.render_engines)``, so it is what a PUBLISHED EPISODE's\r\n  118: #: DURABLE LEDGER can be asked \"which recipe rendered you\". Before this chunk a\r\n  119: #: WAN clip stamped ``recipe: None`` -- there was not even a wrong receipt to\r\n  120: #: catch a drift with. A bare version constant that never reached this string\r\n  121: #: would leave the recipe invisible to every consumer that matters.\r\n  122: RECIPE_WAN_TI2V = \"wan22_ti2v_5b_i2v_single_pass_v1\"\r\n  123: \r\n  124: #: THE CONSENT ACT that re-opens this adapter's recipe knobs. PER ADAPTER, not\r\n  125: #: shared with ``wan_i2v``: one switch for both tiers would stamp a\r\n  126: #: ``+prequalification`` receipt on a clip that had rendered with the frozen\r\n  127: #: recipe, and a receipt that lies in the safer direction still lies.\r\n  128: PREQUALIFICATION_ENV = \"OTR_WAN_TI2V_PREQUALIFICATION\"\r\n  129: \r\n  130: #: THE FROZEN wan_ti2v RECIPE, v1 (LANE 1, 2026-07-27).\r\n  131: #:\r\n  132: #: WHAT v1 IS, STATED HONESTLY: these are TODAY'S SHIPPED DEFAULTS, lifted\r\n  133: #: verbatim from the env fallbacks they replace -- NOT a measured selection.\r\n  134: #: No WAN sweep has run. Freezing them is behaviour-preserving on any box that\r\n  135: #: set nothing, and it is reversible: a prequalification run measures and\r\n  136: #: produces v2 (bump the version INSIDE ``RECIPE_WAN_TI2V`` and add a new dict;\r\n  137: #: never edit a versioned dict in place, or receipts already on disk stop being\r\n  138: #: interpretable).\r\n  139: #:\r\n  140: #: ``max_frames`` IS DELIBERATELY NOT HERE. It is a render-length CEILING, and\r\n  141: #: unlike the ltx tier's it is a LIVE SHIPPED CHANNEL: ``otr_8gb_wan.json`` sets\r\n  142: #: both ``launch.env.OTR_WAN_TI2V_MAX_FRAMES`` and ``video.max_render_frames``.\r\n  143: #: Folding it into the recipe would silently retire the 8GB tier's launch\r\n  144: #: contract (``PBUG-20260723-02``, the bug this freeze descends from).\r\n  145: WAN_TI2V_RECIPE_V1 = {\r\n  146:     \"steps\": 30,\r\n  147:     \"cfg\": 5.0,\r\n  148:     #: ModelSamplingSD3 sigma shift; 5.0 is the 5B value (the 14B uses 8.0).\r\n  149:     \"shift\": 5.0,\r\n  150:     \"sampler\": \"euler\",\r\n  151:     \"scheduler\": \"simple\",\r\n  152:     #: The negative conditioning text. A RENDER INPUT, so it belongs here for\r\n  153:     #: the same reason the samplers do: read from ``os.environ`` it made two\r\n  154:     #: boxes produce visibly different clips that both stamped the same receipt.\r\n  155:     #: This adapter has no per-shot negative channel -- ``_build_graph`` reads\r\n  156:     #: only this -- so before the freeze the server's boot was its SOLE author.\r\n  157:     \"negative\": _WAN_DEFAULT_NEGATIVE,\r\n  158:     #: Tiled decode is ON for this tier: the video-VAE decode is a top VRAM-peak\r\n  159:     #: driver at 8GB. (The ltx tier measured the same direction on 2026-07-27 --\r\n  160:     #: tiled holds the peak FLAT across clip length where untiled climbs with it.\r\n  161:     #: That is ltx's measurement, not this adapter's, so it is context for a\r\n  162:     #: future WAN sweep and not a claim about these numbers.)\r\n  163:     \"tiled_vae\": True,\r\n  164:     #: The tiled-decode geometry, frozen with the flag that reaches it: the day\r\n  165:     #: a measured v2 changes tiling is the day four boot-environment values\r\n  166:     #: would otherwise start deciding what a published clip looks like.\r\n  167:     \"vae_tile\": 256,\r\n  168:     \"vae_overlap\": 64,\r\n  169:     \"vae_temporal\": 16,\r\n  170:     \"vae_temporal_overlap\": 8,\r\n  171: }\r\n  172: \r\n  173: #: THE ONE NAME EVERY CONSUMER READS. Bumping a recipe is repointing this and\r\n  174: #: the version inside ``RECIPE_WAN_TI2V`` -- never editing a versioned dict.\r\n  175: WAN_TI2V_RECIPE = WAN_TI2V_RECIPE_V1\r\n  176: \r\n  177: #: The env var each frozen field was read from, kept so the demotion can NAME\r\n  178: #: what it is ignoring. Presence is all this map is used for outside the consent\r\n  179: #: act -- see ``wan_recipe.ignored_override_keys``.\r\n  180: _RECIPE_ENV_KEYS = {\r\n  181:     \"steps\": \"OTR_WAN_TI2V_STEPS\",\r\n  182:     \"cfg\": \"OTR_WAN_TI2V_CFG\",\r\n  183:     \"shift\": \"OTR_WAN_TI2V_SHIFT\",\r\n  184:     \"sampler\": \"OTR_WAN_TI2V_SAMPLER\",\r\n  185:     \"scheduler\": \"OTR_WAN_TI2V_SCHEDULER\",\r\n  186:     \"negative\": \"OTR_WAN_TI2V_NEGATIVE\",\r\n  187:     \"tiled_vae\": \"OTR_WAN_TI2V_TILED_VAE\",\r\n  188:     \"vae_tile\": \"OTR_WAN_TI2V_VAE_TILE\",\r\n  189:     \"vae_overlap\": \"OTR_WAN_TI2V_VAE_OVERLAP\",\r\n  190:     \"vae_temporal\": \"OTR_WAN_TI2V_VAE_TEMPORAL\",\r\n  191:     \"vae_temporal_overlap\": \"OTR_WAN_TI2V_VAE_TEMPORAL_OVERLAP\",\r\n  192: }\r\n  193: \r\n  194: \r\n  195: #: S1 (2026-07-25) per-model still plan for wan_ti2v (spec section 3,\r\n  196: #: Shape A -- scene spine). FILE-LOCAL, fully declared (no cross-module\r\n  197: #: sharing per the spec's \"no inheritance or shared defaults\" rule).\r\n  198: #: scene_open + scene_beat + scene_character all WIDE + required=always;\r\n  199: #: portrait per subject at the engine's aspect (inherit_engine), not\r\n  200: #: required. Nothing reads the plan at S1 -- S2 wires it in.\r\n  201: _WAN_TI2V_STILL_PLAN = (\r\n  202:     StillPlanRow(kind=\"scene_open\", cardinality=\"per_beat\",\r\n  203:                  target_class=\"scene\", aspect=\"wide\", required=\"always\",\r\n  204:                  framing_geometry=(\r\n  205:                      \"full-frame macro, centered subject\"),\r\n  206:                  style_tail_policy=\"full\"),\r\n  207:     StillPlanRow(kind=\"scene_beat\", cardinality=\"per_beat\",\r\n  208:                  target_class=\"scene\", aspect=\"wide\", required=\"always\",\r\n  209:                  framing_geometry=(\r\n  210:                      (\"cinematic three-quarter framing, people shown with \"\r\n  211:                       \"full heads and clear headroom inside frame, faces \"\r\n  212:                       \"unobstructed, balanced composition\")),\r\n  213:                  style_tail_policy=\"full\"),\r\n  214:     StillPlanRow(kind=\"scene_character\", cardinality=\"per_beat\",\r\n  215:                  target_class=\"scene\", aspect=\"wide\", required=\"always\",\r\n  216:                  framing_geometry=(\r\n  217:                      (\"cinematic medium shot, the character framed within a \"\r\n  218:                       \"wide 16:9 environment, full head and shoulders with \"\r\n  219:                       \"clear headroom inside frame, face unobstructed, \"\r\n  220:                       \"balanced landscape composition\")),\r\n  221:                  style_tail_policy=\"full\"),\r\n  222:     StillPlanRow(kind=\"portrait\", cardinality=\"per_subject\",\r\n  223:                  target_class=\"portrait\", aspect=\"inherit_engine\",\r\n  224:                  required=\"never\",\r\n  225:                  framing_geometry=(\"in-character cinematic medium shot, head \"\r\n  226:                                    \"and shoulders, face clearly visible, \"\r\n  227:                                    \"subject centred with natural headroom \"\r\n  228:                                    \"above the head (never crop the top of the \"\r\n  229:                                    \"head)\"),\r\n  230:                  style_tail_policy=\"full\"),\r\n  231: )\r\n  232: \r\n  233: \r\n  234: @register\r\n  235: class WanTi2vEngine(_WS.WanInitImageMixin, _MC.MotionEngineBase):\r\n  236:     \"\"\"The wan_ti2v 5B image->video adapter (8GB tier; in-process, sidecar_optional).\"\"\"\r\n  237: \r\n  238:     name = \"wan_ti2v\"\r\n  239:     family = \"image_to_video\"\r\n  240:     #: Still-aspect identity (2026-06-17): Wan TI2V renders 16:9, so the director\r\n  241:     #: mints a WIDE init still (non-HuMo, non-mesh-portrait).\r\n  242:     render_aspect = \"wide\"\r\n  243:     #: S1 per-model still plan (see ``_WAN_TI2V_STILL_PLAN`` above).\r\n  244:     still_plan = _WAN_TI2V_STILL_PLAN\r\n  245:     # FLEXIBLE (operator 2026-06-18): eligible for EVERY role -- role_compat is the\r\n  246:     # real gate (it admits wan_ti2v only where the role supplies the required\r\n  247:     # init_image: announcer/music/character/retired_role_a do; the pure background_\r\n  248:     # abstract floor does not, so it's correctly excluded there). Opening `roles`\r\n  249:     # lets the operator pick wan_ti2v for the announcer slot (it animates that beat's\r\n  250:     # selected still); the required_inputs check still prevents a truly broken pick.\r\n  251:     roles = ROLES\r\n  252:     default_roles = ()\r\n  253:     required_inputs = (\"init_image\",)\r\n  254:     #: THE FRAME LADDER (chunk 7a, 2026-07-26). ``_TI2V_MIN_FRAMES`` /\r\n  255:     #: ``_TI2V_MAX_FRAMES`` are this adapter's own named constants; the 4-frame\r\n  256:     #: quantum is Wan's 4n+1 latent stride (17 = 4*4+1, 177 = 4*44+1).\r\n  257:     #: CONTINUITY: the graph wires LoadImage -> Wan22ImageToVideoLatent\r\n  258:     #: ``start_image``, a hard first-frame lock.\r\n  259:     frame_contract = FrameContract(\r\n  260:         min_frames=_TI2V_MIN_FRAMES,\r\n  261:         max_frames=_TI2V_MAX_FRAMES,\r\n  262:         quantum=4,\r\n  263:         native_fps=25,\r\n  264:         allow_tail_trim=True,\r\n  265:         continuity=CONTINUITY_STRICT_FIRST_FRAME,\r\n  266:     )\r\n  267:     commercial_clean = True             # GGUF + VAE are Apache-2.0 (see MODEL_MANIFEST)\r\n  268:     requires_flag = None  # vestigial (registry IS the menu; no flag gate)\r\n  269:     engine_version = \"1\"\r\n  270:     declared_isolation = _MC.ISOLATION_SIDECAR_OPTIONAL\r\n  271:     target_fps = 25\r\n  272:     #: Floor sampler/scheduler whitelist (2026-06-18 roundtable): only core, rock-\r\n  273:     #: solid CROSS-PLATFORM choices -- uni_pc/sa_solver/MoEKSampler are NVIDIA-leaning\r\n  274:     #: / custom / NaN-prone on MPS. assert_usable fails closed on anything else; the\r\n  275:     #: default below is IN the whitelist (so an unset env passes -- no self-reject).\r\n  276:     _PORTABLE_SAMPLERS = frozenset({\"euler\"})\r\n  277:     _PORTABLE_SCHEDULERS = frozenset({\"simple\", \"beta\", \"normal\"})\r\n  278:     _DEFAULT_SAMPLER = \"euler\"\r\n  279:     _DEFAULT_SCHEDULER = \"simple\"\r\n  280: \r\n  281:     # ---- config resolution (env override -> box default) ----\r\n  282:     def _ckpt_path(self):\r\n  283:         return os.environ.get(\"OTR_WAN_TI2V_CKPT\") or os.path.join(\r\n  284:             _COMFY_ROOT, \"models\", \"diffusion_models\", _TI2V_DEFAULT_UNET)\r\n  285: \r\n  286:     def _installed(self):\r\n  287:         \"\"\"The 5B UNET is present if the explicit path exists OR folder_paths\r\n  288:         resolves its basename (the GGUF lives in C:\\\\ComfyUI-Models via\r\n  289:         extra_model_paths, not under the comfy root's models/).\"\"\"\r\n  290:         if os.path.exists(self._ckpt_path()):\r\n  291:             return True\r\n  292:         return self._resolve_model_file(\r\n  293:             (\"diffusion_models\", \"unet\"), self._loader_names()[\"unet\"],\r\n  294:             \"OTR_WAN_TI2V_UNET_DIR\") is not None\r\n  295: \r\n  296:     def resolve_isolation(self):\r\n  297:         \"\"\"``in_process`` by default; escalates to ``sidecar_required`` when\r\n  298:         SageAttention is resident (BUG-070). Pure.\"\"\"\r\n  299:         return _MC.resolve_isolation(\r\n  300:             self.declared_isolation, _MC.sageattention_patched())\r\n  301: \r\n  302:     # ---- usability (fail-closed BEFORE any forward; no heavy import) ----\r\n  303:     def _aux_loader_files(self):\r\n  304:         \"\"\"(label, folder_paths categories, basename, dir-override env) for the\r\n  305:         REQUIRED aux graph loaders beyond the UNET ckpt: the umt5 CLIP and the\r\n  306:         Wan2.2 VAE (M6).\"\"\"\r\n  307:         names = self._loader_names()\r\n  308:         return (\r\n  309:             (\"CLIP/umt5\", (\"text_encoders\", \"clip\"), names[\"clip\"],\r\n  310:              \"OTR_WAN_TI2V_CLIP_DIR\"),\r\n  311:             (\"VAE\", (\"vae\",), names[\"vae\"], \"OTR_WAN_TI2V_VAE_DIR\"),\r\n  312:         )\r\n  313: \r\n  314:     def assert_usable(self, host_caps, profile, request_template=None):\r\n  315:         \"\"\"Fail closed before any forward: the UNET ckpt, the M8 Wan2.2-VAE\r\n  316:         guard, then ALL aux graph loaders (umt5 CLIP + the 2.2 VAE) present on\r\n  317:         disk.\"\"\"\r\n  318:         # Fail CLOSED on a bad/non-portable render knob (sampler whitelist + env\r\n  319:         # range-checks) BEFORE any forward -- never a raw crash mid-render.\r\n  320:         self._resolve_render_config()\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command '$n=0; Get-Content -LiteralPath '\"'nodes/_otr_video_engines/coverage_plan.py' | ForEach-Object { \"'$n++; if($n -ge 1 -and $n -le 280) { '\"'{0,5}: {1}' -f \"'$n,$_ } }'","aggregated_output":"    1: \"\"\"THE PARTITIONER: how many real clips cover one beat, and exactly how long.\r\n    2: \r\n    3: Multi-clip beat coverage (2026-07-25, chunk 3). The operator's requirement is\r\n    4: that a beat be covered by enough REAL rendered clips to be moving video --\r\n    5: chain (segment N+1 begins on segment N's terminal frame) preferred, jump cut\r\n    6: acceptable, and NEVER a mirror/ping-pong or a held last frame.\r\n    7: \r\n    8: PURE AND STATIC. This module reads no environment, no VRAM, no clock, and no\r\n    9: registry. It takes a beat's visible frame target and one\r\n   10: :class:`~.frame_contract.FrameContract` and returns a :class:`CoveragePlan`.\r\n   11: That is a hard requirement, not a style preference: stills are minted BEFORE\r\n   12: the render phase, so a partition that depended on runtime state would be one\r\n   13: the image phase could not have planned stills for.\r\n   14: \r\n   15: THE SEAM ARITHMETIC, which is the subtle part. Under CHAIN the successor's\r\n   16: first frame IS the predecessor's terminal frame, so concatenating both whole\r\n   17: would show that frame twice. Each successor therefore drops its head frame,\r\n   18: and the invariant every plan must satisfy is::\r\n   19: \r\n   20:     sum(render_frames - drop_head - trim_tail) == target_visible_frames\r\n   21: \r\n   22: exactly. Not approximately. A beat whose assembled length drifts from its\r\n   23: audio is the defect this build exists to remove, so an inexact plan is a\r\n   24: terminal error rather than a rounding.\r\n   25: \r\n   26: WHY A SEARCH AND NOT A GREEDY WALK. Legal lengths form the arithmetic ladder\r\n   27: ``min + k*quantum``, so taking the largest legal chunk first can strand a\r\n   28: remainder that is not itself legal (an ``8n+1`` engine covering 170 visible\r\n   29: frames strands 1 frame, and 1 is not a legal render). Solving for the segment\r\n   30: COUNT first always finds an exact partition when one exists.\r\n   31: \"\"\"\r\n   32: \r\n   33: from __future__ import annotations\r\n   34: \r\n   35: from dataclasses import dataclass, field\r\n   36: \r\n   37: from .frame_contract import (\r\n   38:     CONTINUITY_STRICT_FIRST_FRAME,\r\n   39:     FrameContract,\r\n   40: )\r\n   41: \r\n   42: #: Segment N+1 begins exactly on segment N's terminal frame. Preferred.\r\n   43: JOIN_CHAIN = \"chain\"\r\n   44: #: Segments are independent renders butted together. Legal and honest for any\r\n   45: #: engine that cannot lock frame 0.\r\n   46: JOIN_JUMP = \"jump\"\r\n   47: #: One render, the whole beat. Every single_only engine.\r\n   48: JOIN_SINGLE = \"single\"\r\n   49: \r\n   50: JOIN_MODES = (JOIN_CHAIN, JOIN_JUMP, JOIN_SINGLE)\r\n   51: \r\n   52: \r\n   53: class CoveragePlanError(ValueError):\r\n   54:     \"\"\"A beat cannot be covered exactly by this adapter's frame contract.\"\"\"\r\n   55: \r\n   56: \r\n   57: @dataclass(frozen=True)\r\n   58: class CoverageSegment:\r\n   59:     \"\"\"One real render call inside a beat.\r\n   60: \r\n   61:     ``render_frames``  what the adapter is asked to render (always legal).\r\n   62:     ``drop_head``      frames removed from the FRONT at assembly. 1 for a\r\n   63:                        chained successor (it duplicates its predecessor's\r\n   64:                        terminal frame), else 0.\r\n   65:     ``trim_tail``      frames removed from the END at assembly. Non-zero only\r\n   66:                        when the contract allows tail trimming and the ladder\r\n   67:                        cannot land on the target exactly.\r\n   68:     ``index``          0-based position within the beat.\r\n   69:     \"\"\"\r\n   70: \r\n   71:     index: int\r\n   72:     render_frames: int\r\n   73:     drop_head: int = 0\r\n   74:     trim_tail: int = 0\r\n   75: \r\n   76:     @property\r\n   77:     def visible_frames(self) -> int:\r\n   78:         \"\"\"What this segment actually contributes to the assembled beat.\"\"\"\r\n   79:         return int(self.render_frames) - int(self.drop_head) - int(self.trim_tail)\r\n   80: \r\n   81: \r\n   82: @dataclass(frozen=True)\r\n   83: class CoveragePlan:\r\n   84:     \"\"\"The complete, durable description of how one beat gets covered.\"\"\"\r\n   85: \r\n   86:     target_visible_frames: int\r\n   87:     join_mode: str\r\n   88:     segments: tuple = field(default_factory=tuple)\r\n   89: \r\n   90:     @property\r\n   91:     def segment_count(self) -> int:\r\n   92:         return len(self.segments)\r\n   93: \r\n   94:     @property\r\n   95:     def total_visible_frames(self) -> int:\r\n   96:         return sum(s.visible_frames for s in self.segments)\r\n   97: \r\n   98:     @property\r\n   99:     def is_multi_clip(self) -> bool:\r\n  100:         return len(self.segments) > 1\r\n  101: \r\n  102:     def to_dict(self) -> dict:\r\n  103:         \"\"\"JSON-safe form for the durable ledger stamp.\"\"\"\r\n  104:         return {\r\n  105:             \"target_visible_frames\": int(self.target_visible_frames),\r\n  106:             \"join_mode\": str(self.join_mode),\r\n  107:             \"segments\": [\r\n  108:                 {\"index\": int(s.index), \"render_frames\": int(s.render_frames),\r\n  109:                  \"drop_head\": int(s.drop_head), \"trim_tail\": int(s.trim_tail)}\r\n  110:                 for s in self.segments\r\n  111:             ],\r\n  112:         }\r\n  113: \r\n  114:     @classmethod\r\n  115:     def from_dict(cls, data) -> \"CoveragePlan\":\r\n  116:         data = data or {}\r\n  117:         return cls(\r\n  118:             target_visible_frames=int(data.get(\"target_visible_frames\") or 0),\r\n  119:             join_mode=str(data.get(\"join_mode\") or JOIN_SINGLE),\r\n  120:             segments=tuple(\r\n  121:                 CoverageSegment(\r\n  122:                     index=int(row.get(\"index\") or 0),\r\n  123:                     render_frames=int(row.get(\"render_frames\") or 0),\r\n  124:                     drop_head=int(row.get(\"drop_head\") or 0),\r\n  125:                     trim_tail=int(row.get(\"trim_tail\") or 0),\r\n  126:                 )\r\n  127:                 for row in (data.get(\"segments\") or ())\r\n  128:             ),\r\n  129:         )\r\n  130: \r\n  131: \r\n  132: def join_mode_for(contract: FrameContract, target_visible_frames: int) -> str:\r\n  133:     \"\"\"Which join a beat gets, from the adapter's own declaration.\r\n  134: \r\n  135:     ``single`` whenever the beat fits in ONE legal render. Only\r\n  136:     ``strict_first_frame`` earns a chain: a soft identity reference (HuMo) or\r\n  137:     interpolation endpoints (Veo ``lastFrame``) do not lock frame 0, so those\r\n  138:     lanes jump-cut rather than pretend.\r\n  139: \r\n  140:     THE OPT-IN IS GONE (chunk 7a, 2026-07-26). This used to open with\r\n  141:     ``if not contract.supports_multi_clip: return JOIN_SINGLE`` -- every engine\r\n  142:     was single_only until it individually proved otherwise. The operator's\r\n  143:     ruling ended that: \"there's no gate with opt in or opt out... I don't like\r\n  144:     any hidden opt-ins. It either works or it fails.\"\r\n  145: \r\n  146:     The half-measure was worse than either end state, and a QA panel proved it\r\n  147:     on real code: once engines declared real ceilings while the opt-in stayed\r\n  148:     shut, an ordinary 8-second beat on wan_i2v (max 177 frames) had no legal\r\n  149:     single render AND no multi-clip escape, so ``partition_beat`` refused and\r\n  150:     took the whole episode's plan-build down with it. Declaring a ceiling\r\n  151:     without granting the second clip removes the fallback and withholds the\r\n  152:     replacement. The two belong in one change.\r\n  153:     \"\"\"\r\n  154:     target = int(target_visible_frames)\r\n  155:     if contract.is_legal_length(target):\r\n  156:         return JOIN_SINGLE\r\n  157:     # Fits inside ONE render but not on the ladder -- still one clip, with the\r\n  158:     # tail trim covering the remainder. The existence check is load-bearing\r\n  159:     # (2026-07-25 QA): this used to return SINGLE whenever the target was\r\n  160:     # merely <= max_frames, but the smallest legal length AT OR ABOVE the\r\n  161:     # target can still exceed the ceiling. A min=1 quantum=2 max=12 engine\r\n  162:     # asked for 12 frames has no single legal render (the ladder is odd:\r\n  163:     # 1,3,..,11) yet 11 + 1 covers it exactly as two clips -- and the old test\r\n  164:     # declared it SINGLE, then refused it. Found by a differential sweep after\r\n  165:     # the first two math fixes, missed by the panel.\r\n  166:     if contract.allow_tail_trim \\\r\n  167:             and contract.smallest_legal_at_least(target) is not None:\r\n  168:         return JOIN_SINGLE\r\n  169:     return (JOIN_CHAIN\r\n  170:             if contract.continuity == CONTINUITY_STRICT_FIRST_FRAME\r\n  171:             else JOIN_JUMP)\r\n  172: \r\n  173: \r\n  174: def _ladder_partition(total_render_frames, contract, count):\r\n  175:     \"\"\"Split ``total_render_frames`` into exactly ``count`` legal lengths.\r\n  176: \r\n  177:     Legal lengths are ``min + quantum*a`` with ``0 <= a <= a_max``, so a split\r\n  178:     exists iff the residue is divisible by ``quantum`` and the required number\r\n  179:     of quantum steps fits inside ``count`` segments. Fills each segment toward\r\n  180:     the ceiling in order, which keeps the plan deterministic and puts the short\r\n  181:     segment last -- where a viewer expects a beat to end.\r\n  182:     \"\"\"\r\n  183:     min_f, q = int(contract.min_frames), int(contract.quantum)\r\n  184:     residue = int(total_render_frames) - count * min_f\r\n  185:     if residue < 0 or residue % q:\r\n  186:         return None\r\n  187:     steps = residue // q\r\n  188:     max_steps_each = (((int(contract.max_frames) - min_f) // q)\r\n  189:                       if contract.max_frames else steps)\r\n  190:     if max_steps_each < 0 or steps > count * max_steps_each:\r\n  191:         return None\r\n  192:     out = []\r\n  193:     for _ in range(count):\r\n  194:         take = min(steps, max_steps_each)\r\n  195:         out.append(min_f + take * q)\r\n  196:         steps -= take\r\n  197:     return out\r\n  198: \r\n  199: \r\n  200: def _candidate_totals(required, contract, count):\r\n  201:     \"\"\"Total render values worth trying for a TRIMMED cover, cheapest first.\r\n  202: \r\n  203:     For a ladder contract the total of ``count`` legal lengths is always\r\n  204:     ``count*min + quantum*A``, so the reachable totals are exactly the values\r\n  205:     congruent to ``count*min`` modulo ``quantum`` and bounded by ``count*max``.\r\n  206:     That makes the smallest total at or above ``required`` fully determined --\r\n  207:     exactly one candidate, nothing to guess.\r\n  208: \r\n  209:     A discrete menu is not an arithmetic progression, so there the reachable\r\n  210:     totals are scanned upward. The scan is bounded by the largest menu entry:\r\n  211:     trimming more than one whole segment's worth would mean the last segment\r\n  212:     contributes nothing, which the validator rejects anyway.\r\n  213:     \"\"\"\r\n  214:     required = int(required)\r\n  215:     if contract.discrete_frames:\r\n  216:         span = max(int(d) for d in contract.discrete_frames)\r\n  217:         ceiling = count * span\r\n  218:         return range(required, min(required + span, ceiling) + 1)\r\n  219:     min_f, q = int(contract.min_frames), int(contract.quantum)\r\n  220:     base = count * min_f\r\n  221:     total = base if required <= base else (\r\n  222:         base + -(-(required - base) // q) * q)        # ceil to the next step\r\n  223:     if contract.max_frames and total > count * int(contract.max_frames):\r\n  224:         return ()\r\n  225:     return (total,)\r\n  226: \r\n  227: \r\n  228: def _discrete_partition(total_render_frames, contract, count):\r\n  229:     \"\"\"Exact split over a fixed duration menu (Veo's 4/6/8s), or None.\r\n  230: \r\n  231:     MEMOIZED, and that is not an optimization -- it is a correctness-of-service\r\n  232:     fix (2026-07-25 QA). The bare recursive descent explores up to\r\n  233:     ``len(menu) ** count`` nodes, so with a four-value menu it took 18s at\r\n  234:     count=14 and was still running past 20s at count=16. Since\r\n  235:     :func:`partition_beat` walks counts up to ``max_segments`` (64), an\r\n  236:     unsatisfiable target would hang the calling thread indefinitely rather than\r\n  237:     refuse -- a render node that never returns is worse than one that fails.\r\n  238:     Memoizing on ``(remaining, left)`` bounds the search to\r\n  239:     ``total * count`` states, which is small and predictable.\r\n  240:     \"\"\"\r\n  241:     menu = sorted({int(d) for d in contract.discrete_frames}, reverse=True)\r\n  242:     if not menu:\r\n  243:         return None\r\n  244:     smallest = menu[-1]\r\n  245:     memo = {}\r\n  246: \r\n  247:     def _walk(remaining, left):\r\n  248:         if left == 0:\r\n  249:             return [] if remaining == 0 else None\r\n  250:         # Bound the branch before recursing: `left` segments can cover at most\r\n  251:         # left*largest and at least left*smallest.\r\n  252:         if remaining < left * smallest or remaining > left * menu[0]:\r\n  253:             return None\r\n  254:         key = (remaining, left)\r\n  255:         if key in memo:\r\n  256:             return memo[key]\r\n  257:         result = None\r\n  258:         for value in menu:\r\n  259:             if value > remaining:\r\n  260:                 continue\r\n  261:             rest = _walk(remaining - value, left - 1)\r\n  262:             if rest is not None:\r\n  263:                 result = [value] + rest\r\n  264:                 break\r\n  265:         memo[key] = result\r\n  266:         return result\r\n  267: \r\n  268:     return _walk(int(total_render_frames), count)\r\n  269: \r\n  270: \r\n  271: def partition_beat(target_visible_frames, contract, *, join_mode=None,\r\n  272:                    max_segments=64) -> CoveragePlan:\r\n  273:     \"\"\"THE ENTRY POINT: cover ``target_visible_frames`` exactly.\r\n  274: \r\n  275:     Raises :class:`CoveragePlanError` when no exact cover exists, rather than\r\n  276:     returning a plan whose assembled length would drift from the beat's audio.\r\n  277:     \"\"\"\r\n  278:     target = int(target_visible_frames)\r\n  279:     if target < 1:\r\n  280:         raise CoveragePlanError(\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command '$n=0; Get-Content -LiteralPath '\"'nodes/otr_credits_roll.py' | ForEach-Object { \"'$n++; if($n -ge 1125 -and $n -le 1470) { '\"'{0,5}: {1}' -f \"'$n,$_ } }'","aggregated_output":" 1125:     for y in range(0, base.size[1], 4):\r\n 1126:         sd.line([(0, y), (base.size[0], y)], fill=(0, 0, 0, 66))\r\n 1127:     return Image.alpha_composite(base, sl)\r\n 1128: \r\n 1129: \r\n 1130: # =========================================================================== #\r\n 1131: # Duration + backdrop\r\n 1132: # =========================================================================== #\r\n 1133: def compute_credits_duration_s(roll_px: int, view_h: int,\r\n 1134:                                pps: float = _SCROLL_PPS) -> tuple:\r\n 1135:     \"\"\"Returns (dur_s, effective_pps) for the CLASSIC credits roll.\r\n 1136: \r\n 1137:     ``roll_px`` = the full travel distance of the col-3 canvas (content_h +\r\n 1138:     view_h): the content enters from BELOW the viewport and fully exits above\r\n 1139:     it, so EVERY line passes through the viewport -- nothing is ever clipped,\r\n 1140:     and it ALWAYS rolls regardless of transcript length (roundtable R1: the old\r\n 1141:     overflow-only ``content_h - view_h`` model left short episodes static +\r\n 1142:     clipped). Over the ceiling -> SPEED UP (never truncate).\"\"\"\r\n 1143:     if pps <= 0:\r\n 1144:         raise CreditsDataError(f\"pps must be > 0 (got {pps})\")\r\n 1145:     roll_px = max(1, int(roll_px))\r\n 1146:     dur = _LEAD_HOLD_S + roll_px / pps + _TAIL_HOLD_S\r\n 1147:     eff = pps\r\n 1148:     if dur > _MAX_HOLD_S:\r\n 1149:         eff = roll_px / max(1.0, _MAX_HOLD_S - _LEAD_HOLD_S - _TAIL_HOLD_S)\r\n 1150:         dur = _MAX_HOLD_S\r\n 1151:     return (round(dur, 3), eff)\r\n 1152: \r\n 1153: \r\n 1154: def extract_final_frame(video_path: str, out_png: str) -> str:\r\n 1155:     \"\"\"The backdrop: the BODY VIDEO's own final frame, frozen.\r\n 1156: \r\n 1157:     REPLACES ``plan_backdrop`` (2026-07-29, WIRE-W6), which hunted the clip\r\n 1158:     manifest for the last loopable FILE clip and raised when it found none.\r\n 1159: \r\n 1160:     THE DEFECT THAT KILLED: it excluded DIRECTORY clips, because ffmpeg\r\n 1161:     ``-stream_loop -1 -i <dir>`` crashes -- and ``mesh_stage`` writes a frame\r\n 1162:     directory rather than an mp4. So an episode rendered ENTIRELY by mesh_stage\r\n 1163:     had no file clip at all, and the terminal node of the graph refused the\r\n 1164:     whole finished episode. It rendered 7 of 7 shots and published nothing. Not\r\n 1165:     a regression -- true since 2026-07-03, and found by the 2026-07-28\r\n 1166:     engine-coverage campaign.\r\n 1167: \r\n 1168:     THE FIX IS TO STOP LOOKING THERE. ``otr_silent_composite`` has ALREADY\r\n 1169:     flattened every directory clip into the assembled body video by the time\r\n 1170:     this node runs, so the body video is a complete, always-present, always-mp4\r\n 1171:     record of the same pixels -- and it is already this node's own input. One\r\n 1172:     source instead of two. CreditsRoll no longer knows what a directory clip\r\n 1173:     is, and cannot be broken again by a new clip KIND it has never heard of.\r\n 1174: \r\n 1175:     LOOK DELTA, STATED PLAINLY BECAUSE IT IS VISIBLE: the operator's 2026-06-17\r\n 1176:     contract said the console rides over the last drama clip LOOPED. It now\r\n 1177:     rides over that clip's final frame HELD. Still drama, still darkened, still\r\n 1178:     never black -- but motionless for the length of the roll. Ratified in the\r\n 1179:     2026-07-28 wiring arc (r3, unamended by r4); flagged here for an eyeball\r\n 1180:     because a panel cannot judge how a 52-second held frame reads.\r\n 1181: \r\n 1182:     ``-sseof -3`` seeks three seconds from the END and takes the last frame\r\n 1183:     that decodes, which is robust on a container whose duration metadata is\r\n 1184:     approximate. RAISES: a body video whose final frame cannot be read is not\r\n 1185:     a presentation problem, it is an unreadable body.\r\n 1186:     \"\"\"\r\n 1187:     cmd = [_ffmpeg_bin(), \"-y\", \"-sseof\", \"-3\", \"-i\", video_path,\r\n 1188:            \"-update\", \"1\", \"-frames:v\", \"1\", \"-q:v\", \"2\", out_png]\r\n 1189:     r = subprocess.run(cmd, capture_output=True, text=True)\r\n 1190:     if r.returncode != 0 or not os.path.exists(out_png) \\\r\n 1191:             or os.path.getsize(out_png) == 0:\r\n 1192:         # A very short body may have nothing 3s from the end; take frame 0.\r\n 1193:         r = subprocess.run(\r\n 1194:             [_ffmpeg_bin(), \"-y\", \"-i\", video_path,\r\n 1195:              \"-update\", \"1\", \"-frames:v\", \"1\", \"-q:v\", \"2\", out_png],\r\n 1196:             capture_output=True, text=True)\r\n 1197:     if r.returncode != 0 or not os.path.exists(out_png) \\\r\n 1198:             or os.path.getsize(out_png) == 0:\r\n 1199:         raise CreditsDataError(\r\n 1200:             \"could not extract a backdrop frame from the body video %r \"\r\n 1201:             \"(rc=%s): %s\" % (video_path, r.returncode, (r.stderr or \"\")[-500:]))\r\n 1202:     return out_png\r\n 1203: \r\n 1204: \r\n 1205: # =========================================================================== #\r\n 1206: # ffmpeg render + append (every failure RAISES; no source-copy)\r\n 1207: # =========================================================================== #\r\n 1208: def _ffmpeg_bin() -> str:\r\n 1209:     # Honor OTR_FFMPEG (the sibling video nodes' config path) before PATH, so\r\n 1210:     # credits never fail on a box where ffmpeg is configured but not on PATH.\r\n 1211:     cand = (os.environ.get(\"OTR_FFMPEG\") or \"\").strip()\r\n 1212:     p = (cand if (cand and (os.path.isfile(cand) or shutil.which(cand)))\r\n 1213:          else shutil.which(\"ffmpeg\"))\r\n 1214:     if not p:\r\n 1215:         raise CreditsDataError(\r\n 1216:             \"ffmpeg not found (OTR_FFMPEG / PATH) -- cannot render credits\")\r\n 1217:     return p\r\n 1218: \r\n 1219: \r\n 1220: def _ffprobe_bin() -> str:\r\n 1221:     cand = (os.environ.get(\"OTR_FFPROBE\") or \"\").strip()\r\n 1222:     p = (cand if (cand and (os.path.isfile(cand) or shutil.which(cand)))\r\n 1223:          else shutil.which(\"ffprobe\"))\r\n 1224:     if not p:\r\n 1225:         raise CreditsDataError(\r\n 1226:             \"ffprobe not found (OTR_FFPROBE / PATH) -- cannot render credits\")\r\n 1227:     return p\r\n 1228: \r\n 1229: \r\n 1230: def _probe_video(path: str) -> dict:\r\n 1231:     out = subprocess.run(\r\n 1232:         [_ffprobe_bin(), \"-v\", \"error\", \"-select_streams\", \"v:0\",\r\n 1233:          \"-show_entries\", \"stream=width,height,r_frame_rate\",\r\n 1234:          \"-show_entries\", \"format=duration\", \"-of\", \"json\", path],\r\n 1235:         capture_output=True, text=True)\r\n 1236:     if out.returncode != 0:\r\n 1237:         raise CreditsDataError(f\"ffprobe failed on {path!r}: {out.stderr}\")\r\n 1238:     data = json.loads(out.stdout or \"{}\")\r\n 1239:     st = (data.get(\"streams\") or [{}])[0]\r\n 1240:     num, _, den = str(st.get(\"r_frame_rate\") or \"25/1\").partition(\"/\")\r\n 1241:     fps = float(num) / float(den or 1)\r\n 1242:     try:\r\n 1243:         dur = float((data.get(\"format\") or {}).get(\"duration\") or 0.0)\r\n 1244:     except (TypeError, ValueError):\r\n 1245:         dur = 0.0\r\n 1246:     return {\"w\": int(st.get(\"width\") or 0), \"h\": int(st.get(\"height\") or 0),\r\n 1247:             \"fps\": fps, \"duration\": dur}\r\n 1248: \r\n 1249: \r\n 1250: def render_credits_clip(layout: dict, backdrop_path: str, out_path: str,\r\n 1251:                         *, w: int, h: int, fps: float) -> float:\r\n 1252:     \"\"\"Render the SILENT credits console clip: static base (cols 1-2) + the\r\n 1253:     scrolling col-3 canvas, over the LOOPED darkened backdrop, with a fade in/out.\r\n 1254:     Returns the clip duration (== declared credits tail). RAISES on any failure.\"\"\"\r\n 1255:     base_img = render_static_base(layout, w, h)\r\n 1256:     scroll_img = render_scroll_canvas(layout[\"col3_flow\"],\r\n 1257:                                       _sc(_COL3_W, h), h)\r\n 1258:     col3_x = _sc(_COL3_X, h)\r\n 1259:     col3_y = _sc(_COL3_VIEW_Y, h)\r\n 1260:     view_h = min(_sc(_COL3_VIEW_H, h), h - col3_y - _sc(40, h))\r\n 1261:     # CLASSIC ROLL (roundtable R1 fix): pad the scroll canvas view_h transparent\r\n 1262:     # at TOP and BOTTOM so the content ENTERS from below the viewport and EXITS\r\n 1263:     # above the top -- EVERY line passes through the viewport, nothing is ever\r\n 1264:     # clipped, and it ALWAYS rolls regardless of transcript length. The crop\r\n 1265:     # window travels y = 0 .. roll_px where roll_px = content_h + view_h.\r\n 1266:     from PIL import Image as _Image\r\n 1267:     _padded = _Image.new(\r\n 1268:         \"RGBA\", (scroll_img.width, scroll_img.height + 2 * view_h), (0, 0, 0, 0))\r\n 1269:     _padded.paste(scroll_img, (0, view_h))\r\n 1270:     scroll_img = _padded\r\n 1271:     roll_px = scroll_img.height - view_h            # = content_h + view_h\r\n 1272:     dur, eff_pps = compute_credits_duration_s(roll_px, view_h)\r\n 1273: \r\n 1274:     base_png = out_path + \".base.png\"\r\n 1275:     scroll_png = out_path + \".scroll.png\"\r\n 1276:     base_img.convert(\"RGBA\").save(base_png)\r\n 1277:     scroll_img.convert(\"RGBA\").save(scroll_png)\r\n 1278:     try:\r\n 1279:         yexpr = \"clip((t-%.3f)*%.4f\\\\,0\\\\,%d)\" % (_LEAD_HOLD_S, eff_pps, roll_px)\r\n 1280:         fade_out_st = max(0.0, dur - _FADE_OUT_S)\r\n 1281:         cmd = [\r\n 1282:             _ffmpeg_bin(), \"-y\",\r\n 1283:             # The backdrop is a STILL (the body video's frozen final frame --\r\n 1284:             # see `extract_final_frame`), so it is looped like the other two\r\n 1285:             # image inputs rather than `-stream_loop`ed like a clip. It still\r\n 1286:             # feeds the same scale/crop/darken chain below, so the console's\r\n 1287:             # look is unchanged apart from the frame being held.\r\n 1288:             \"-loop\", \"1\", \"-framerate\", f\"{fps}\", \"-i\", backdrop_path,\r\n 1289:             # base + scroll are STILLS: they MUST be looped image inputs at the clip\r\n 1290:             # fps so each carries an advancing per-frame timestamp. Fed as a plain\r\n 1291:             # `-i <png>` they are a SINGLE frame at t=0, so the col-3 crop y-expr\r\n 1292:             # (which scrolls on `t`) is frozen at y=0 -> the blank top pad, and the\r\n 1293:             # whole scroll column renders empty for the entire roll (the shipped bug).\r\n 1294:             \"-loop\", \"1\", \"-framerate\", f\"{fps}\", \"-i\", base_png,\r\n 1295:             \"-loop\", \"1\", \"-framerate\", f\"{fps}\", \"-i\", scroll_png,\r\n 1296:             \"-filter_complex\",\r\n 1297:             (f\"[0:v]scale={w}:{h}:force_original_aspect_ratio=increase,\"\r\n 1298:              f\"crop={w}:{h},eq=brightness=-0.32,fps={fps}[bg];\"\r\n 1299:              f\"[bg][1:v]overlay=0:0[b1];\"\r\n 1300:              # The crop y-expr scrolls per-frame (this ffmpeg evaluates crop x/y\r\n 1301:              # per frame; proven by the text-scroll test). The REAL fix is the\r\n 1302:              # classic-roll model above (roll_px = content_h + view_h): a large,\r\n 1303:              # length-independent travel so col 3 ALWAYS visibly rolls and nothing\r\n 1304:              # is clipped (the old overflow-only model left short episodes static).\r\n 1305:              f\"[2:v]crop=w={_sc(_COL3_W, h)}:h={view_h}:x=0:y='{yexpr}'[sc];\"\r\n 1306:              f\"[b1][sc]overlay={col3_x}:{col3_y}[cv];\"\r\n 1307:              f\"[cv]fade=t=in:st=0:d={_FADE_IN_S:.2f},\"\r\n 1308:              f\"fade=t=out:st={fade_out_st:.2f}:d={_FADE_OUT_S:.2f}[v]\"),\r\n 1309:             \"-map\", \"[v]\", \"-an\",\r\n 1310:             \"-t\", f\"{dur:.3f}\",\r\n 1311:             \"-c:v\", \"libx264\", \"-pix_fmt\", \"yuv420p\", \"-preset\", \"veryfast\",\r\n 1312:             \"-crf\", \"18\", out_path,\r\n 1313:         ]\r\n 1314:         r = subprocess.run(cmd, capture_output=True, text=True)\r\n 1315:         if r.returncode != 0 or not os.path.exists(out_path) \\\r\n 1316:                 or os.path.getsize(out_path) == 0:\r\n 1317:             raise CreditsDataError(\r\n 1318:                 f\"credits console render failed (rc={r.returncode}): \"\r\n 1319:                 f\"{(r.stderr or '')[-1000:]}\")\r\n 1320:     finally:\r\n 1321:         for p in (base_png, scroll_png):\r\n 1322:             try:\r\n 1323:                 os.remove(p)\r\n 1324:             except OSError:\r\n 1325:                 pass\r\n 1326:     return dur\r\n 1327: \r\n 1328: \r\n 1329: def append_credits(body_path: str, credits_path: str, out_path: str) -> str:\r\n 1330:     \"\"\"Concat body + credits (both silent, matching params) via the concat\r\n 1331:     demuxer, stream-copy. NO source-copy fallback: any failure RAISES.\"\"\"\r\n 1332:     if not os.path.exists(body_path):\r\n 1333:         raise CreditsDataError(f\"body video missing: {body_path!r}\")\r\n 1334:     if not os.path.exists(credits_path):\r\n 1335:         raise CreditsDataError(f\"credits clip missing: {credits_path!r}\")\r\n 1336:     lst = out_path + \".concat.txt\"\r\n 1337:     with open(lst, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\r\n 1338:         for p in (body_path, credits_path):\r\n 1339:             f.write(\"file '%s'\\n\" % p.replace(\"\\\\\", \"/\").replace(\"'\", r\"'\\''\"))\r\n 1340:     try:\r\n 1341:         r = subprocess.run(\r\n 1342:             [_ffmpeg_bin(), \"-y\", \"-f\", \"concat\", \"-safe\", \"0\", \"-i\", lst,\r\n 1343:              \"-c\", \"copy\", out_path],\r\n 1344:             capture_output=True, text=True)\r\n 1345:         if r.returncode != 0 or not os.path.exists(out_path) \\\r\n 1346:                 or os.path.getsize(out_path) == 0:\r\n 1347:             raise CreditsDataError(\r\n 1348:                 f\"credits append (concat) failed (rc={r.returncode}): \"\r\n 1349:                 f\"{(r.stderr or '')[-800:]}\")\r\n 1350:     finally:\r\n 1351:         try:\r\n 1352:             os.remove(lst)\r\n 1353:         except OSError:\r\n 1354:             pass\r\n 1355:     return out_path\r\n 1356: \r\n 1357: \r\n 1358: # =========================================================================== #\r\n 1359: # The terminal node (wired 93 -> OTR_CreditsRoll -> 85)\r\n 1360: # =========================================================================== #\r\n 1361: class OTRCreditsRoll:\r\n 1362:     \"\"\"Registered as ``OTR_CreditsRoll``. Appends the late SIGNAL LOST console\r\n 1363:     to node 93's output and hands the mux (85) the video path + the DECLARED\r\n 1364:     credits-tail duration (credits-aware guard).\"\"\"\r\n 1365: \r\n 1366:     CATEGORY = \"OldTimeRadio/v2/video\"\r\n 1367:     FUNCTION = \"roll\"\r\n 1368:     RETURN_TYPES = (\"STRING\", \"FLOAT\", \"STRING\")\r\n 1369:     RETURN_NAMES = (\"video_with_credits_path\", \"declared_credits_tail_s\",\r\n 1370:                     \"report\")\r\n 1371:     OUTPUT_NODE = False\r\n 1372: \r\n 1373:     @classmethod\r\n 1374:     def INPUT_TYPES(cls):\r\n 1375:         return {\"required\": {\r\n 1376:             \"video_path\": (\"STRING\", {\r\n 1377:                 \"forceInput\": True,\r\n 1378:                 \"tooltip\": \"Node 93 output (captions/bars already burned).\"}),\r\n 1379:             \"clip_manifest_json\": (\"STRING\", {\r\n 1380:                 \"forceInput\": True,\r\n 1381:                 \"tooltip\": \"Node 92 slot 1 (third fan-out consumer).\"}),\r\n 1382:         }}\r\n 1383: \r\n 1384:     def roll(self, video_path, clip_manifest_json):\r\n 1385:         from .production_ledger import get_ledger\r\n 1386: \r\n 1387:         if not video_path or not os.path.exists(video_path):\r\n 1388:             raise CreditsDataError(\r\n 1389:                 f\"credits input video missing: {video_path!r}\")\r\n 1390:         try:\r\n 1391:             manifest = json.loads(clip_manifest_json or \"\")\r\n 1392:         except (TypeError, ValueError) as exc:\r\n 1393:             raise CreditsDataError(\r\n 1394:                 f\"clip_manifest_json unparseable: {exc}\") from exc\r\n 1395: \r\n 1396:         # ---- TERMINAL: the body, and the TRUTH the card is a view of ------ #\r\n 1397:         #\r\n 1398:         # THE BOUNDARY (wiring arc r4/A7, 2026-07-29). This node is the LAST\r\n 1399:         # one in the graph, so everything it raises costs a whole rendered\r\n 1400:         # episode. But it may not simply never fail, because the standing\r\n 1401:         # policy is that the card is a VIEW OF THE DURABLE LEDGER, not the\r\n 1402:         # ledger: a record may never elide. So the two halves are split.\r\n 1403:         #\r\n 1404:         # Above this line is TRUTH. An unreadable body, a malformed manifest,\r\n 1405:         # a ledger missing a receipt the card is obliged to show -- these stay\r\n 1406:         # terminal, and `build_credits_layout` keeps raising exactly as it did.\r\n 1407:         # Degrading here would publish an episode whose credits silently claim\r\n 1408:         # less than the build actually knows, which is the one failure this\r\n 1409:         # card exists to prevent.\r\n 1410:         led = get_ledger()\r\n 1411:         vp = _probe_video(video_path)\r\n 1412:         w = vp[\"w\"] or 1920\r\n 1413:         h = vp[\"h\"] or 1080\r\n 1414:         layout = build_credits_layout(led.data, w=w, h=h, manifest=manifest)\r\n 1415: \r\n 1416:         base, ext = os.path.splitext(video_path)\r\n 1417:         credits_clip = base + \"_credits\" + (ext or \".mp4\")\r\n 1418:         backdrop_png = base + \"_credits_backdrop.png\"\r\n 1419:         out = base + \"_with_credits\" + (ext or \".mp4\")\r\n 1420: \r\n 1421:         # ---- PRESENTATION-ONLY: everything that makes GLASS ---------------- #\r\n 1422:         #\r\n 1423:         # Below this line is glass. Frame extraction, the dim/overlay, the\r\n 1424:         # console composition and its encode all produce a PICTURE of truth\r\n 1425:         # already established above. If any of them fails, the honest outcome\r\n 1426:         # is the finished episode WITHOUT a credits tail plus a receipt saying\r\n 1427:         # so -- never the loss of the episode. `declared_credits_tail_s` goes\r\n 1428:         # to 0.0 so the downstream mux's credits-aware guard is told the truth\r\n 1429:         # about what it is receiving, and the report carries ok=False with the\r\n 1430:         # reason rather than a cheerful default.\r\n 1431:         try:\r\n 1432:             extract_final_frame(video_path, backdrop_png)\r\n 1433:             tail_s = render_credits_clip(\r\n 1434:                 layout, backdrop_png, credits_clip, w=w, h=h, fps=vp[\"fps\"])\r\n 1435:             append_credits(video_path, credits_clip, out)\r\n 1436:         except Exception as exc:                      # noqa: BLE001 -- see above\r\n 1437:             log.error(\r\n 1438:                 \"[OTR_CreditsRoll] PRESENTATION FAILURE -- returning the \"\r\n 1439:                 \"finished body with NO credits tail rather than losing the \"\r\n 1440:                 \"episode: %s\", exc)\r\n 1441:             return (video_path, 0.0, json.dumps({\r\n 1442:                 \"ok\": False, \"declared_credits_tail_s\": 0.0,\r\n 1443:                 \"credits_rendered\": False,\r\n 1444:                 \"reason\": \"presentation_failure\",\r\n 1445:                 \"error\": str(exc)[:500],\r\n 1446:                 \"hero\": layout[\"hero\"], \"output\": video_path},\r\n 1447:                 ensure_ascii=True))\r\n 1448:         finally:\r\n 1449:             try:\r\n 1450:                 os.remove(backdrop_png)\r\n 1451:             except OSError:\r\n 1452:                 pass\r\n 1453: \r\n 1454:         report = json.dumps({\r\n 1455:             \"ok\": True, \"declared_credits_tail_s\": round(tail_s, 3),\r\n 1456:             \"credits_rendered\": True,\r\n 1457:             \"hero\": layout[\"hero\"], \"cols\": [len(layout[\"col1\"]),\r\n 1458:                                              len(layout[\"col3_flow\"])],\r\n 1459:             \"backdrop_source\": \"body_final_frame\", \"output\": out},\r\n 1460:             ensure_ascii=True)\r\n 1461:         log.info(\"[OTR_CreditsRoll] appended %.1fs console (hero=%r backdrop=\"\r\n 1462:                  \"body final frame) -> %s\", tail_s, layout[\"hero\"], out)\r\n 1463:         return (out, float(tail_s), report)\r\n 1464: \r\n 1465: \r\n 1466: __all__ = [\r\n 1467:     \"OTRCreditsRoll\", \"CreditsDataError\", \"build_credits_layout\",\r\n 1468:     \"compute_credits_duration_s\", \"extract_final_frame\", \"render_static_base\",\r\n 1469:     \"render_scroll_canvas\", \"render_credits_clip\", \"append_credits\",\r\n 1470: ]\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command '$n=0; Get-Content -LiteralPath '\"'nodes/otr_silent_composite.py' | ForEach-Object { \"'$n++; if($n -ge 390 -and $n -le 800) { '\"'{0,5}: {1}' -f \"'$n,$_ } }'","aggregated_output":"  390:                     next_start, requested_n, timeline_end)\r\n  391:                 continue\r\n  392:             if r.get(\"exists\") and r.get(\"path\"):\r\n  393:                 _fill = _should_loop_fill(r, n)\r\n  394:                 _warn_clip_underrun(r, n, will_loop=_fill)\r\n  395:                 emit(\"clip\", r.get(\"path\"), n, 0, r.get(\"shot_id\"),\r\n  396:                      r.get(\"engine_id\"), loop=_fill,\r\n  397:                      bg_still_path=r.get(\"bg_still_path\"))\r\n  398:             else:\r\n  399:                 emit(gap_src, \"\", n, _floor_aligned(cursor, n),\r\n  400:                      r.get(\"shot_id\"), r.get(\"engine_id\"))\r\n  401:             cursor = slot_end\r\n  402:     else:                                                  # SEQUENTIAL (legacy)\r\n  403:         for r in rows:\r\n  404:             n = int(r.get(\"target_frame_count\") or 0)\r\n  405:             if r.get(\"exists\") and r.get(\"path\"):\r\n  406:                 _fill = _should_loop_fill(r, n)\r\n  407:                 _warn_clip_underrun(r, n, will_loop=_fill)\r\n  408:                 emit(\"clip\", r.get(\"path\"), n, 0, r.get(\"shot_id\"),\r\n  409:                      r.get(\"engine_id\"), loop=_fill,\r\n  410:                      bg_still_path=r.get(\"bg_still_path\"))\r\n  411:             elif floor_available:\r\n  412:                 start = min(cursor, max(0, ff - n)) if ff else cursor\r\n  413:                 emit(\"floor\", \"\", n, start, r.get(\"shot_id\"), r.get(\"engine_id\"))\r\n  414:             else:\r\n  415:                 emit(\"black\", \"\", n, 0, r.get(\"shot_id\"), r.get(\"engine_id\"))\r\n  416:             cursor += n\r\n  417:     if target_total_frames is not None and int(target_total_frames) > cursor:\r\n  418:         # Tail to the master length (the closing-theme region, A/V-sync). Hold\r\n  419:         # the LAST drama clip on screen as the backdrop (operator 2026-06-17\r\n  420:         # \"credits over the scene\" look): a short clip loops, a long one plays\r\n  421:         # its head; fall back to the procgen END-slice / black when there is no\r\n  422:         # real clip. NOTE (credits enrichment 2026-07-03): this fills only to the\r\n  423:         # MASTER length; the credits POST-ROLL past the master (the old BUG-410\r\n  424:         # floor-extend) is GONE -- the unified credits roll is now a SILENT tail\r\n  425:         # appended LATE by OTR_CreditsRoll. It used to reproduce this\r\n  426:         # looped-last-clip backdrop by re-reading the clip manifest; since\r\n  427:         # 2026-07-29 (WIRE-W6) it freezes the final frame of the body video\r\n  428:         # THIS function assembles, so the manifest has exactly one reader.\r\n  429:         tail_n = int(target_total_frames) - cursor\r\n  430:         _clip_rows = [r for r in rows if r.get(\"exists\") and r.get(\"path\")]\r\n  431:         if positioned:\r\n  432:             _last_clip = (max(_clip_rows, key=lambda r: float(r.get(\"start_s\") or 0))\r\n  433:                           if _clip_rows else None)\r\n  434:         else:\r\n  435:             _last_clip = _clip_rows[-1] if _clip_rows else None\r\n  436:         if _last_clip is not None:\r\n  437:             emit(\"clip\", _last_clip.get(\"path\"), tail_n, 0,\r\n  438:                  _last_clip.get(\"shot_id\"), _last_clip.get(\"engine_id\"), loop=True,\r\n  439:                  bg_still_path=_last_clip.get(\"bg_still_path\"))\r\n  440:         else:\r\n  441:             emit(gap_src, \"\", tail_n, _floor_aligned(cursor, tail_n))\r\n  442:         cursor = int(target_total_frames)\r\n  443:     return segments, cursor\r\n  444: \r\n  445: \r\n  446: def timeline_quality_report(manifest, segments):\r\n  447:     \"\"\"S-A legibility floor (staged commit 1): a SEPARATE post-plan view that\r\n  448:     asserts each real-clip beat DELIVERS its planned visible span and flags any\r\n  449:     beat that would freeze. PURE -- never overwrites the raw manifest\r\n  450:     ``frame_count`` (which stays engine-produced); it only reads the planned\r\n  451:     segments.\r\n  452: \r\n  453:     In positioned mode, a later beat owns its start boundary, so intentional\r\n  454:     crossfade overlap frames are trimmed from the earlier beat's visible slot.\r\n  455:     ``target_frame_count`` remains the full render request; the added\r\n  456:     ``planned_visible_frame_count`` and ``overlap_trimmed_frame_count`` make the\r\n  457:     distinction explicit. ``delivered_frames_ok`` is True when NO visible slot\r\n  458:     is held on an under-length clip. Sequential manifests retain their strict\r\n  459:     delivered == requested contract.\"\"\"\r\n  460:     clips = {str(r.get(\"shot_id\")): r\r\n  461:              for r in ((manifest or {}).get(\"clips\") or [])\r\n  462:              if r.get(\"shot_id\") and int((r or {}).get(\"target_frame_count\") or 0) > 0}\r\n  463:     positioned = (bool(clips)\r\n  464:                   and int((manifest or {}).get(\"total_target_frames\") or 0) > 0\r\n  465:                   and all(r.get(\"start_s\") is not None for r in clips.values()))\r\n  466:     seg_by_shot = {}\r\n  467:     for s in (segments or []):\r\n  468:         if s.get(\"source\") == \"clip\" and s.get(\"shot_id\"):\r\n  469:             seg_by_shot.setdefault(str(s[\"shot_id\"]), []).append(s)\r\n  470:     beats = []\r\n  471:     ok_all = True\r\n  472:     for sid, r in clips.items():\r\n  473:         tgt = int(r.get(\"target_frame_count\") or 0)\r\n  474:         raw = int(r.get(\"frame_count\") or 0)\r\n  475:         segs = seg_by_shot.get(sid, [])\r\n  476:         delivered = sum(int(s.get(\"n_frames\") or 0) for s in segs)\r\n  477:         planned_visible = delivered\r\n  478:         looped = any(s.get(\"loop\") for s in segs)\r\n  479:         if not segs:\r\n  480:             status = \"no_clip_segment\"\r\n  481:         elif raw > 0 and raw < planned_visible:\r\n  482:             status = \"looped_fill\" if looped else \"held_last_frame\"\r\n  483:         else:\r\n  484:             status = \"ok\"\r\n  485:         beats.append({\r\n  486:             \"shot_id\": sid, \"beat_id\": r.get(\"beat_id\"),\r\n  487:             \"engine_id\": r.get(\"engine_id\"), \"target_frame_count\": tgt,\r\n  488:             \"requested_frame_count\": tgt, \"frame_count\": raw,\r\n  489:             \"rendered_frame_count\": raw,\r\n  490:             \"delivered_frame_count\": delivered,\r\n  491:             \"planned_visible_frame_count\": planned_visible,\r\n  492:             \"overlap_trimmed_frame_count\": (\r\n  493:                 max(0, tgt - planned_visible) if positioned else 0),\r\n  494:             \"looped\": bool(looped), \"quality_status\": status})\r\n  495:         if status == \"held_last_frame\":\r\n  496:             ok_all = False\r\n  497:         elif not positioned and segs and delivered != tgt:\r\n  498:             ok_all = False\r\n  499:     return {\"delivered_frames_ok\": ok_all, \"beats\": beats,\r\n  500:             \"underran\": [b for b in beats\r\n  501:                          if b[\"quality_status\"] in (\"looped_fill\", \"held_last_frame\")]}\r\n  502: \r\n  503: \r\n  504: _FREEZE_RE = None\r\n  505: \r\n  506: \r\n  507: def parse_freezedetect(stderr):\r\n  508:     \"\"\"Parse ffmpeg ``freezedetect`` stderr into a list of frozen spans\r\n  509:     ``[{start, end}]`` (seconds). PURE -- offline-testable. An open\r\n  510:     freeze_start with no freeze_end (frozen through EOF) yields end=None.\"\"\"\r\n  511:     global _FREEZE_RE\r\n  512:     if _FREEZE_RE is None:\r\n  513:         import re\r\n  514:         _FREEZE_RE = re.compile(\r\n  515:             r\"lavfi\\.freezedetect\\.freeze_(start|end)[:=]\\s*([0-9.]+)\")\r\n  516:     spans = []\r\n  517:     cur = None\r\n  518:     for tag, val in _FREEZE_RE.findall(stderr or \"\"):\r\n  519:         v = float(val)\r\n  520:         if tag == \"start\":\r\n  521:             cur = {\"start\": v, \"end\": None}\r\n  522:             spans.append(cur)\r\n  523:         elif tag == \"end\" and cur is not None:\r\n  524:             cur[\"end\"] = v\r\n  525:             cur = None\r\n  526:     return spans\r\n  527: \r\n  528: \r\n  529: def freezedetect_silent(video_path, *, ffmpeg=\"ffmpeg\", noise_db=-60, dur_s=2.0):\r\n  530:     \"\"\"Run ffmpeg ``freezedetect`` over the SILENT video only (never the master)\r\n  531:     and return the parsed frozen spans. Used by the S-A live legibility proof;\r\n  532:     NOT wired into the default assemble path (it adds a full decode pass).\r\n  533:     FAIL-SOFT: returns ``[]`` if ffmpeg is unavailable.\"\"\"\r\n  534:     fb = _ffmpeg_bin(ffmpeg)\r\n  535:     if not fb or not os.path.isfile(video_path):\r\n  536:         return []\r\n  537:     p = _run([fb, \"-hide_banner\", \"-i\", video_path, \"-vf\",\r\n  538:               \"freezedetect=n=%ddB:d=%s\" % (int(noise_db), str(dur_s)),\r\n  539:               \"-map\", \"0:v:0\", \"-f\", \"null\", os.devnull])\r\n  540:     return parse_freezedetect((p.stderr or \"\") + (p.stdout or \"\"))\r\n  541: \r\n  542: \r\n  543: def _seg_vf(w, h, fps, start_frame, sharpen=True):\r\n  544:     \"\"\"The per-segment ``-vf`` chain: an optional source trim, then the SHARED\r\n  545:     scale chain (lanczos+unsharp when ``sharpen``), then the tpad last-frame hold.\r\n  546:     PRESERVES the ``trim -> scale/unsharp/pad/fps -> tpad`` ordering. ``sharpen``\r\n  547:     is True for a real clip (the soft-native fix) and False for the procgen-floor\r\n  548:     slice (byte-identical to the legacy chain).\"\"\"\r\n  549:     trim = (\"trim=start_frame=%d,setpts=PTS-STARTPTS,\" % int(start_frame)) \\\r\n  550:         if int(start_frame) > 0 else \"\"\r\n  551:     return _scale_filter(\r\n  552:         w, h, fps, sharpen=sharpen, pre=trim,\r\n  553:         post=\",tpad=stop_mode=clone:stop_duration=3600\")\r\n  554: \r\n  555: \r\n  556: def _color_args(out_path):\r\n  557:     # TAG bt709 identity (never matrix-convert) + canonical yuv420p H.264.\r\n  558:     return [\"-vsync\", \"cfr\", \"-pix_fmt\", \"yuv420p\",\r\n  559:             \"-color_primaries\", \"bt709\", \"-color_trc\", \"bt709\", \"-colorspace\", \"bt709\",\r\n  560:             \"-c:v\", \"libx264\", \"-crf\", \"18\", \"-preset\", \"fast\", out_path]\r\n  561: \r\n  562: \r\n  563: def _encode_segment(fb, src, n_frames, seg_path, *, w, h, fps, start_frame=0,\r\n  564:                     loop=False, sharpen=True):\r\n  565:     \"\"\"One canonical silent segment of EXACTLY ``n_frames`` from ``src`` (a clip,\r\n  566:     or the floor sliced at ``start_frame``): truncates a long source, holds the\r\n  567:     last frame (tpad clone) for a short one. FAIL CLOSED on ffmpeg error.\r\n  568: \r\n  569:     ``loop=True`` stream-loops the input (-stream_loop -1) so a SHORT source\r\n  570:     REPEATS to fill ``n_frames`` -- the credits-tail backdrop keeps moving\r\n  571:     instead of freezing on the last frame (operator 2026-06-17). The tpad clone\r\n  572:     in _seg_vf stays as a safety but never triggers under an infinite loop.\r\n  573: \r\n  574:     ``sharpen`` is True for a real engine clip (lanczos+unsharp soft-native fix)\r\n  575:     and False for the procgen-floor slice (NOT sharpened -- byte-identical).\"\"\"\r\n  576:     loop_args = [\"-stream_loop\", \"-1\"] if loop else []\r\n  577:     cmd = [fb, \"-y\", \"-loglevel\", \"error\"] + loop_args + [\"-i\", src, \"-an\",\r\n  578:            \"-vf\", _seg_vf(w, h, fps, start_frame, sharpen=sharpen),\r\n  579:            \"-frames:v\", str(int(n_frames))] + _color_args(seg_path)\r\n  580:     p = _run(cmd)\r\n  581:     if p.returncode != 0:\r\n  582:         raise ValueError(\"OTR_SilentComposite: segment encode failed (%s) :: %s\"\r\n  583:                          % (os.path.basename(seg_path), p.stderr.strip()[:200]))\r\n  584: \r\n  585: \r\n  586: def _encode_black(fb, n_frames, seg_path, *, w, h, fps):\r\n  587:     \"\"\"A generated black segment of EXACTLY ``n_frames`` (the ultimate gap-fill\r\n  588:     so an episode with neither a clip nor a floor still assembles).\"\"\"\r\n  589:     cmd = [fb, \"-y\", \"-loglevel\", \"error\",\r\n  590:            \"-f\", \"lavfi\", \"-i\", \"color=c=black:s=%dx%d:r=%d\" % (w, h, fps),\r\n  591:            \"-frames:v\", str(int(n_frames))] + _color_args(seg_path)\r\n  592:     p = _run(cmd)\r\n  593:     if p.returncode != 0:\r\n  594:         raise ValueError(\"OTR_SilentComposite: black segment failed (%s) :: %s\"\r\n  595:                          % (os.path.basename(seg_path), p.stderr.strip()[:200]))\r\n  596: \r\n  597: \r\n  598: # --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #\r\n  599: # Directory-clip read path (3D plan 7.2 -- the character_3d alpha handoff).\r\n  600: # A clip row may point at a DIRECTORY of straight-alpha RGBA frames (PNG/EXR,\r\n  601: # sorted by name) instead of an mp4. The segment encoder lists the frames via\r\n  602: # the shared nodes/_otr_video_engines/directory_clip.py rule, plays them at\r\n  603: # the canonical fps via an ffconcat list (no %06d numbering assumption),\r\n  604: # OVERLAYS them centered on the background (the floor slice when available,\r\n  605: # else black -- the W7 provider-plate composite arrives with the 3D lane),\r\n  606: # and FLATTENS to opaque yuv420p. ffmpeg's overlay expects STRAIGHT\r\n  607: # (non-premultiplied) alpha -- exactly the validated contract. The webm/vp9 /\r\n  608: # mov/prores4444 alpha-VIDEO branches are CUT from v1 [H-RT, GPT].\r\n  609: # --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #\r\n  610: def _is_frame_dir(path) -> bool:\r\n  611:     \"\"\"True when ``path`` is a readable directory-clip frame dir (tolerant).\"\"\"\r\n  612:     try:\r\n  613:         from ._otr_video_engines.directory_clip import frame_dir_summary\r\n  614:     except ImportError:  # pragma: no cover -- flat test imports\r\n  615:         from _otr_video_engines.directory_clip import frame_dir_summary  # type: ignore\r\n  616:     ok, _n, _b = frame_dir_summary(path)\r\n  617:     return ok\r\n  618: \r\n  619: \r\n  620: def _write_frames_concat(frames, listfile, fps):\r\n  621:     \"\"\"An ffconcat v1 list playing each frame for exactly 1/fps seconds\r\n  622:     (sorted-by-name order is the caller's contract).\"\"\"\r\n  623:     with open(listfile, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\r\n  624:         f.write(\"ffconcat version 1.0\\n\")\r\n  625:         for fp in frames:\r\n  626:             f.write(\"file '%s'\\n\" % fp.replace(\"\\\\\", \"/\").replace(\"'\", \"'\\\\''\"))\r\n  627:             f.write(\"duration %.6f\\n\" % (1.0 / float(fps)))\r\n  628:         # concat-demuxer quirk: the LAST entry's duration is honored only if\r\n  629:         # the file is listed once more (else the final frame is dropped early)\r\n  630:         f.write(\"file '%s'\\n\" % frames[-1].replace(\"\\\\\", \"/\").replace(\"'\", \"'\\\\''\"))\r\n  631: \r\n  632: \r\n  633: def _encode_segment_from_dir(fb, frame_dir, n_frames, seg_path, *, w, h, fps,\r\n  634:                              bg_path=\"\", bg_start_frame=0, bg_is_still=False):\r\n  635:     \"\"\"One canonical silent segment of EXACTLY ``n_frames`` from a straight-\r\n  636:     alpha frame DIRECTORY: frames sorted by name -> overlay (centered) on the\r\n  637:     background -> flatten yuv420p. FAIL CLOSED on a bad directory or ffmpeg\r\n  638:     error. ``bg_path`` (the floor) is sliced at ``bg_start_frame``; absent ->\r\n  639:     black.\r\n  640: \r\n  641:     ``bg_is_still=True`` (the textured-hero 3D PoC, C1): ``bg_path`` is a single\r\n  642:     STILL PLATE image, not a video -- it is looped (``-loop 1``) and held for the\r\n  643:     full ``n_frames`` (the generated background behind the turntable mesh). The\r\n  644:     slice ``bg_start_frame`` is irrelevant for a still and ignored.\"\"\"\r\n  645:     try:\r\n  646:         from ._otr_video_engines.directory_clip import list_directory_frames\r\n  647:     except ImportError:  # pragma: no cover -- flat test imports\r\n  648:         from _otr_video_engines.directory_clip import list_directory_frames  # type: ignore\r\n  649:     frames = list_directory_frames(frame_dir)   # raises ValueError, named\r\n  650:     workdir = os.path.dirname(seg_path)\r\n  651:     listfile = os.path.join(\r\n  652:         workdir, os.path.basename(seg_path) + \".frames.ffconcat\")\r\n  653:     _write_frames_concat(frames, listfile, fps)\r\n  654:     if bg_path and os.path.isfile(bg_path) and bg_is_still:\r\n  655:         # A single still plate: loop it to fill the beat (no trim/tpad needed --\r\n  656:         # the loop + the overlay eof_action=repeat hold it for every frame). A\r\n  657:         # REAL still plate IS sharpened (sharpen=True) -- it is composited content,\r\n  658:         # not the procgen floor.\r\n  659:         bg_in = [\"-loop\", \"1\", \"-i\", bg_path]\r\n  660:         bg_filter = _scale_filter(w, h, fps, sharpen=True,\r\n  661:                                   in_label=\"0:v\", out_label=\"bg\")\r\n  662:     elif bg_path and os.path.isfile(bg_path):\r\n  663:         # The procgen-floor video slice -> NOT sharpened (byte-identical to the\r\n  664:         # legacy chain); preserve the trim prefix + tpad hold.\r\n  665:         bg_in = [\"-i\", bg_path]\r\n  666:         trim = ((\"trim=start_frame=%d,setpts=PTS-STARTPTS,\"\r\n  667:                  % int(bg_start_frame)) if int(bg_start_frame) > 0 else \"\")\r\n  668:         bg_filter = _scale_filter(\r\n  669:             w, h, fps, sharpen=False, in_label=\"0:v\", out_label=\"bg\",\r\n  670:             pre=trim, post=\",tpad=stop_mode=clone:stop_duration=3600\")\r\n  671:     else:\r\n  672:         bg_in = [\"-f\", \"lavfi\", \"-i\",\r\n  673:                  \"color=c=black:s=%dx%d:r=%d\" % (w, h, fps)]\r\n  674:         bg_filter = \"[0:v]null[bg]\"\r\n  675:     # FOREGROUND: straight-alpha RGBA -> sharpen=True but pad=False (a black pad\r\n  676:     # would paint opaque borders over the alpha edges -> destroy the matte). The\r\n  677:     # overlay re-centers the fg, so no pad is needed.\r\n  678:     fg_filter = _scale_filter(w, h, fps, sharpen=True, pad=False,\r\n  679:                               in_label=\"1:v\", out_label=\"fg\", pre=\"format=rgba,\")\r\n  680:     # 3D image streams chunk 7: DEFAULT = straight-alpha SOURCE-OVER at FULL\r\n  681:     # opacity. Compositing in RGB (overlay format=rgb) makes an OPAQUE mesh pixel\r\n  682:     # (alpha==255) fully REPLACE the plate -- no premultiplied-edge ghost, no\r\n  683:     # double-exposure of the background plate through the mesh. The mesh already\r\n  684:     # renders straight-alpha, so its own alpha is the matte. The prior auto-format\r\n  685:     # look is preserved as the NAMED opt-in style OTR_MESH_COMPOSITE_STYLE=blend\r\n  686:     # (never the default).\r\n  687:     _style = os.environ.get(\"OTR_MESH_COMPOSITE_STYLE\", \"source_over\").strip().lower()\r\n  688:     _ov_format = \"auto\" if _style == \"blend\" else \"rgb\"\r\n  689:     graph = (bg_filter + \";\" + fg_filter +\r\n  690:              \";[bg][fg]overlay=(W-w)/2:(H-h)/2:eof_action=repeat:format=%s,\"\r\n  691:              \"format=yuv420p\" % _ov_format)\r\n  692:     cmd = [fb, \"-y\", \"-loglevel\", \"error\"] + bg_in + [\r\n  693:         \"-f\", \"concat\", \"-safe\", \"0\", \"-i\", listfile, \"-an\",\r\n  694:         \"-filter_complex\", graph,\r\n  695:         \"-frames:v\", str(int(n_frames))] + _color_args(seg_path)\r\n  696:     p = _run(cmd)\r\n  697:     if p.returncode != 0:\r\n  698:         raise ValueError(\r\n  699:             \"OTR_SilentComposite: directory-clip segment failed (%s) :: %s\"\r\n  700:             % (os.path.basename(seg_path), p.stderr.strip()[:300]))\r\n  701: \r\n  702: \r\n  703: def assemble_silent_timeline(manifest, base_video_path, out_path, *, w=1472,\r\n  704:                              h=832, fps=25, ffmpeg=\"ffmpeg\"):\r\n  705:     \"\"\"Assemble a beat-ordered clip manifest into ONE always-silent canonical\r\n  706:     CFR video; FAIL CLOSED. Sequential beats retain their full requested spans;\r\n  707:     positioned beats are conformed to their non-overlapping visible slots. A\r\n  708:     missing clip is gap-filled from the floor (``base_video_path``) or black.\r\n  709:     The assembled frame count is asserted == the audio-derived timeline boundary\r\n  710:     (the pre-mux A/V sync guard). Returns ``(out_path, report)``.\"\"\"\r\n  711:     report: list = []\r\n  712:     fb = _ffmpeg_bin(ffmpeg)\r\n  713:     if not fb:\r\n  714:         raise ValueError(\"OTR_SilentComposite: ffmpeg not found (%r)\" % ffmpeg)\r\n  715:     w, h, fps = _even(w), _even(h), max(1, int(fps))\r\n  716:     floor_ok = bool(base_video_path) and os.path.isfile(base_video_path)\r\n  717:     floor_frames = count_video_frames(base_video_path) if floor_ok else 0\r\n  718:     # The post-audio ledger's accepted timeline boundary is primary. Positioned\r\n  719:     # manifests may overlap full render requests at audio crossfades, so their\r\n  720:     # render-work sum is deliberately NOT the output length. Legacy/sequential\r\n  721:     # manifests still carry their old requested-frame sum here.\r\n  722:     mft_total = int((manifest or {}).get(\"timeline_total_frames\")\r\n  723:                     or (manifest or {}).get(\"total_target_frames\") or 0)\r\n  724:     target_total = mft_total if mft_total > 0 else None\r\n  725:     _rows = [r for r in ((manifest or {}).get(\"clips\") or [])\r\n  726:              if int((r or {}).get(\"target_frame_count\") or 0) > 0]\r\n  727:     manifest_positioned = (bool(_rows)\r\n  728:                            and all(r.get(\"start_s\") is not None for r in _rows))\r\n  729:     if floor_ok:\r\n  730:         # Cross-check/fallback against the actual MASTER MIX. A positioned\r\n  731:         # manifest may reconcile downward as well as upward: refusing to shrink\r\n  732:         # here was the terminal live failure when two 0.5 s crossfades were\r\n  733:         # counted twice. Sequential/legacy manifests preserve the historical\r\n  734:         # grow-only behavior. Ceil covers the final fractional audio frame; the\r\n  735:         # mux keeps its independent, narrow terminal tolerance.\r\n  736:         master_dur = 0.0\r\n  737:         try:\r\n  738:             import glob as _glob\r\n  739:             _sib = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(base_video_path),\r\n  740:                                 \"*_master.wav\")\r\n  741:             for _cand in _glob.glob(_sib):\r\n  742:                 master_dur = max(master_dur, _probe_audio_duration(_cand))\r\n  743:         except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 -- best-effort; fallbacks below\r\n  744:             pass\r\n  745:         if master_dur <= 0:\r\n  746:             master_dur = _probe_audio_duration(base_video_path)\r\n  747:         if master_dur <= 0:\r\n  748:             master_dur = _probe_duration(base_video_path)\r\n  749:         if master_dur > 0:\r\n  750:             base_total = max(1, int(math.ceil(master_dur * fps)))\r\n  751:             reconcile = (base_total > 0 and (\r\n  752:                 target_total is None\r\n  753:                 or (manifest_positioned and base_total != target_total)\r\n  754:                 or (not manifest_positioned and base_total > target_total)))\r\n  755:             if reconcile:\r\n  756:                 if target_total is not None and manifest_positioned:\r\n  757:                     report.append(\r\n  758:                         \"A/V-sync master reconcile: %d -> %d frames \"\r\n  759:                         \"(positioned ledger cross-check)\"\r\n  760:                         % (target_total, base_total))\r\n  761:                 elif target_total is not None:\r\n  762:                     report.append(\r\n  763:                         \"A/V-sync tail to master: %d -> %d frames \"\r\n  764:                         \"(closing-theme backdrop)\"\r\n  765:                         % (target_total, base_total))\r\n  766:                 target_total = base_total\r\n  767:         # CREDITS FLOOR-EXTEND RIPPED (credits enrichment 2026-07-03, BUG-410\r\n  768:         # retired). This block USED to extend the composite PAST the master to\r\n  769:         # the procgen floor's FULL frame count so ~20s of green rolling credits\r\n  770:         # scrolled in silence after the closing theme (the second \"credits\r\n  771:         # organ\", Fable BUILD-BREAKER #2). Under the silent-tail model the\r\n  772:         # unified credits roll is appended LATE as a SILENT tail by\r\n  773:         # OTR_CreditsRoll (which since 2026-07-29 rides over the FROZEN FINAL\r\n  774:         # FRAME of the body this function assembles, and DECLARES its duration\r\n  775:         # to the credits-aware mux guard). The composite now ends at the MASTER\r\n  776:         # length -- no floor-extend.\r\n  777:     segments, total = plan_timeline_segments(\r\n  778:         manifest, floor_available=floor_ok, floor_frames=floor_frames,\r\n  779:         target_total_frames=target_total, fps=fps)\r\n  780:     if not segments or total <= 0:\r\n  781:         raise ValueError(\"OTR_SilentComposite: manifest has no renderable beats\")\r\n  782:     # S-A legibility floor: a SEPARATE delivered-frames view (raw manifest\r\n  783:     # frame_count untouched). LOUD-report any underran beat + whether clip-fill\r\n  784:     # filled it; a held_last_frame beat (fill OFF) is a legibility failure.\r\n  785:     qa = timeline_quality_report(manifest, segments)\r\n  786:     if qa[\"underran\"]:\r\n  787:         report.append(\r\n  788:             \"clip-fill: %d beat(s) underran -> %s\"\r\n  789:             % (len(qa[\"underran\"]),\r\n  790:                \", \".join(\"%s %s(%d/%d)\"\r\n  791:                          % (b[\"shot_id\"], b[\"quality_status\"],\r\n  792:                             b[\"rendered_frame_count\"],\r\n  793:                             b[\"planned_visible_frame_count\"])\r\n  794:                          for b in qa[\"underran\"])))\r\n  795:     if not qa[\"delivered_frames_ok\"]:\r\n  796:         _held = sum(1 for b in qa[\"beats\"]\r\n  797:                     if b[\"quality_status\"] == \"held_last_frame\")\r\n  798:         report.append(\r\n  799:             \"LEGIBILITY (LOUD): %d beat(s) did NOT deliver planned visible frames \"\r\n  800:             \"(held_last_frame -> static murk); clip-fill is OFF \"\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command '$n=0; Get-Content -LiteralPath '\"'docs/GO_FORWARD_PLAN.md' | ForEach-Object { \"'$n++; if($n -ge 820 -and $n -le 930) { '\"'{0,5}: {1}' -f \"'$n,$_ } }'","aggregated_output":"  820: \r\n  821: - RENDER / qualification windows: local production models + the Codex-app\r\n  822:   monitor; Claude only to launch and wrap.\r\n  823: - CODER windows: Claude codes; rung-1 Qwen triages every failure first; Codex\r\n  824:   only via the two-strikes law.\r\n  825: - PLANNER window: Claude; the sec-16 + r5 kibitz (codex + agy) is THIS WEEK's\r\n  826:   scheduled Codex spend while both pools are fresh -- it is the operator\r\n  827:   bottleneck on the critical path.\r\n  828: - CODER E extensibility (21-31 d): spans multiple credit weeks -- plan wave\r\n  829:   boundaries at the weekly resets; mid-build Codex only via two-strikes.\r\n  830: \r\n  831: ## THE LAW (operator, 2026-07-22 -- supersedes anything that disagrees)\r\n  832: \r\n  833: > **AN AUDIT MAY IMPROVE A STORY. IT MAY NEVER FAIL ONE FOR LENGTH, LANGUAGE,\r\n  834: > STYLE, VISUAL VOCABULARY, OR QUALITY.**\r\n  835: \r\n  836: The sole terminal spoken-prose policy is the shared whole-word safety\r\n  837: authority: profanity, explicit guns/knives/weapons, and explicit\r\n  838: sexual/nudity content. Smoking and benign substrings such as `begun` pass.\r\n  839: Structural JSON/schema/IDs/roster/source-proof/rights/graph/markup/nonempty/\r\n  840: provider-integrity failures remain fail-closed because they protect a usable\r\n  841: ledger rather than judge prose. Across all six banks, requested word length,\r\n  842: actual word count, drift, one-breath estimates, visual/world vocabulary,\r\n  843: noun/POS heuristics, casing/title/honorific style, craft, and quality are\r\n  844: guidance or telemetry only -- they may never reject, reroll, retire, replace,\r\n  845: or block an episode. Same-story LLM cleanup is allowed.\r\n  846: \r\n  847: ## CURRENT STEP -- **WIRE THE SIX NO_RENDER LOCAL ENGINES. WIRE-W1, W2 and W6\r\n  848: ## ARE LANDED AND PUSHED; WIRE-W3 (WAN) is the next line of code.**\r\n  849: \r\n  850: **LANDED 2026-07-29 (CODER window, HEAD == origin `a14ecdfa`; suite\r\n  851: 7551 passed / 27 skipped / 1 xfailed; Bible 17; `build_variants --check` 11\r\n  852: variants / 0 failures; canonical `9872624A` byte-identical across all three --\r\n  853: no node, widget, link or schema touched by any of them):**\r\n  854: \r\n  855: - **`5efd2baf` WIRE-W1** -- the partitioner takes the FEWEST legal clips. It\r\n  856:   ran two walks over the segment count (every count for an EXACT cover, then\r\n  857:   every count again for a TRIMMED one), so an exact cover at a HIGH count beat\r\n  858:   a trimmed cover at a LOW one. Now one walk: exact, then a permitted trim,\r\n  859:   then advance. Measured over 798,510 (contract, target) pairs across 2,538\r\n  860:   contract shapes -- **46,949 plans changed, EVERY ONE a segment-count\r\n  861:   reduction, zero refusals introduced, zero count increases.** `184 ->\r\n  862:   [153, 33]` trim 2, and 185-240 all two segments, as codex pinned.\r\n  863: - **`a218b1f7` WIRE-W2** -- a cast-time image gap DECLARES itself.\r\n  864:   `DeferredImageGapError(RenderError)` in the new dependency-leaf\r\n  865:   `nodes/_otr_video_engines/render_errors.py`; `RenderError` moved with it and\r\n  866:   is re-exported from `render_driver`. Five cast-time sites raise it (one was a\r\n  867:   bare `ValueError` -- that is why r3's `:1985` was not in the RenderError\r\n  868:   list); the three post-image still-spine gaps and both wrong-aspect failures\r\n  869:   stay terminal. **Both fail-open swallows in ShotLock are gone.**\r\n  870: - **`a14ecdfa` WIRE-W6** -- the end card rides the body video's frozen final\r\n  871:   frame; `plan_backdrop` is DELETED. Terminal/presentation boundary per r4/A7.\r\n  872: - **`3e89d6b2` WIRE-W3a** -- `wan_i2v` gets its beat session. `session_identity()`\r\n  873:   AND the UNET-only hoist in ONE commit, because codex's r3 warning is real:\r\n  874:   the identity alone silences `SessionIdentityUnavailable` and the segment\r\n  875:   graph still runs `UNETLoader` every segment. **Measured: a 3-segment beat\r\n  876:   loads the UNET once and the CLIP/VAE three times each** -- the auxiliaries\r\n  877:   reloading is the NARROWED contract (\"primary diffusion patcher once per\r\n  878:   beat; auxiliaries may reload\"), not a shortfall, because `free_after_use`\r\n  879:   keeping umt5 and the 14B out of co-residency is the only thing between this\r\n  880:   lane and an OOM at 14,499 MB. Receipt mechanism shared in `wan_shared`, data\r\n  881:   per adapter. Suite 7561; mutation 7/7.\r\n  882: \r\n  883: **WIRE-W3b IS THE NEXT LINE OF CODE, and it is NOT just a copy of W3a.** The\r\n  884: session half mirrors `eng_wan_i2v` almost exactly (identity, UNET-only\r\n  885: `prepare`, `external_results` in `_build_graph` + `render_clip`, `teardown`\r\n  886: dropping the handles first -- `_wan_session_receipts()` already works for it).\r\n  887: The half that is NEW is the ping-pong:\r\n  888: \r\n  889: - `eng_wan_ti2v._floor_length` (`:551`) floors the render to what live VRAM\r\n  890:   affords, and `render_clip` (`:725-733`) PING-PONG EXTENDS that short render\r\n  891:   up to the beat target. `coverage_plan`'s module docstring forbids exactly\r\n  892:   that for a planned multi-clip beat.\r\n  893: - **Do NOT rip it.** It is load-bearing for the shipped 8 GB WAN tier\r\n  894:   (`PBUG-20260723-02`): WAN renders a short native clip on purpose and fills\r\n  895:   the beat with it. Suppress it ONLY for a coverage-planned segment, the way\r\n  896:   `eng_ltx_8gb` does, and leave the single-clip path alone.\r\n  897: - Record `native_frame_count` and the extension MODE on every receipt so the\r\n  898:   W5 grader can reject ping-pong on a lane claiming real multi-clip.\r\n  899: - Compute the native budget AFTER prepared-model residency (r3): with the UNET\r\n  900:   already hoisted, `free_vram_mb()` reads a different number than it did when\r\n  901:   the loader ran inside the segment graph, so the budget must be taken with\r\n  902:   the same memory state every segment sees.\r\n  903: \r\n  904: **ONE OPERATOR EYEBALL OWED, and it is the only thing WIRE-W6 cannot settle\r\n  905: itself:** the credits console used to ride the last drama clip LOOPED; it now\r\n  906: rides that clip's final frame HELD, for the length of the roll. Same darkened\r\n  907: drama imagery, never credits-over-black -- but motionless. Ratified in r3 and\r\n  908: unamended by r4, and it is what removes the manifest read that made an\r\n  909: all-`mesh_stage` episode unpublishable. If the held frame reads badly, the fix\r\n  910: is a short looped tail cut FROM THE BODY rather than a return to the manifest.\r\n  911: \r\n  912: **ONE NEW OPEN ROW, filed not built (see OPEN BUGS):** the fewest-segments\r\n  913: preference can accept a disproportionate trim on a discrete menu whose largest\r\n  914: entry dwarfs its smallest. A bound was written, MEASURED and REVERTED -- it\r\n  915: cost more than it saved on real ladders. No shipped contract can produce the\r\n  916: pathological case.\r\n  917: \r\n  918: **A TRAP THAT COST A RED HEAD, worth knowing before the next chunk:** the B7\r\n  919: forbidden sweep (`tests/test_b7_forbidden_sweep.py`) diffs **tracked** files\r\n  920: only, so a brand-new test file passes the gate while untracked and fails the\r\n  921: commit AFTER it lands. It flags `alias` as a runtime identifier. Fixed in\r\n  922: `a14ecdfa`; run the full suite once more after the first commit of any new\r\n  923: test file.\r\n  924: \r\n  925: **THIS IS NOT LEAN-MEAN, AND LEAN-MEAN IS NOT ON THIS DOCUMENT.** Operator\r\n  926: direction 2026-07-29 moved LEAN-MEAN FRONT and TAIL to the Lean-mean campaign\r\n  927: section of `ROADMAP.md`, where they sit behind SFX and product expansion. A\r\n  928: window that opens on lean-mean has read a stale list -- see the struck-through\r\n  929: 2026-07-24 rescope, and the voided CODER D / CODER G rows. **This plan's order\r\n  930: is: LOCAL-ENGINE OBS WIRING -> WAN 8-GB -> Randomizer A -> `dynamic_story` ->\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_32","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command '$n=0; Get-Content -LiteralPath '\"'docs/HANDOFF_LOG.md' | ForEach-Object { \"'$n++; if($n -ge 1 -and $n -le 100) { '\"'{0,5}: {1}' -f \"'$n,$_ } }'","aggregated_output":"    1: # OTR Handoff Log\r\n    2: \r\n    3: Append-only session log, newest at top. What each session actually did;\r\n    4: GO_FORWARD_PLAN.md stays lean and forward-only.\r\n    5: \r\n    6: ## 2026-07-29 -- HEAD 3e89d6b2 (v2.0-alpha) -- WINDOW CODER (wiring block, cont.)\r\n    7: Did: **WIRE-W3a `3e89d6b2`** -- wan_i2v's beat session. session_identity() and\r\n    8:   the UNET-only hoist in ONE commit, because codex's r3 warning is real: the\r\n    9:   identity alone silences BeatSession's refusal and the segment graph still\r\n   10:   runs UNETLoader every segment, so the beat would look fixed and reload a 14B\r\n   11:   three times. Acceptance counts LOADER INVOCATIONS, never prepare() calls --\r\n   12:   BeatSession carries no counters for exactly that reason. Measured: 3-segment\r\n   13:   beat = 1 UNET load, 3 CLIP loads, 3 VAE loads. The auxiliaries reloading IS\r\n   14:   the narrowed contract; hoisting the CLIP would pin ~9 GB and delete the\r\n   15:   free_after_use mitigation that keeps this lane off a 14,499 MB peak.\r\n   16:   Identity carries the recipe, the loader MODE and a size+mtime receipt for\r\n   17:   every loader file INCLUDING the un-hoisted CLIP and VAE (r4/A5 -- TI2V\r\n   18:   distinguishes incompatible VAE generations). Receipt mechanism shared in\r\n   19:   wan_shared, data per adapter; eng_ltx_8gb keeps its own copy on purpose.\r\n   20:   Suite 7561 / 27 / 1; Bible 17; canonical 9872624A; mutation 7/7 with M1\r\n   21:   being the trap itself.\r\n   22: Current step: WIRE-W3b (wan_ti2v). The session half mirrors wan_i2v almost\r\n   23:   exactly; the NEW half is the ping-pong -- _floor_length + the extend at\r\n   24:   render_clip:725-733 must be suppressed for a COVERAGE-PLANNED segment only\r\n   25:   (it stays load-bearing for the shipped 8GB tier, PBUG-20260723-02), the\r\n   26:   native frame count and extension mode go on every receipt, and the native\r\n   27:   budget is computed AFTER prepared-model residency.\r\n   28: Next: WIRE-W3b -> WIRE-W4 -> WIRE-W7 -> WIRE-W5, then the 45-word run over all\r\n   29:   18 local video/still engines. NOTHING in this block is live-proven yet.\r\n   30: Models: Claude (rung 4) only. No Codex spend -- two-strikes never fired.\r\n   31: Commits: 3e89d6b2 (+ this handoff).\r\n   32: \r\n   33: ## 2026-07-29 -- HEAD a14ecdfa (v2.0-alpha) -- WINDOW CODER (wiring block)\r\n   34: Did: WIRE-W1, WIRE-W2 and WIRE-W6 built, gated and pushed, one green chunk at\r\n   35:   a time, from r3/final.md as amended by r4/final.md.\r\n   36:   **WIRE-W1 `5efd2baf`** -- partition_beat ran TWO walks over the segment count\r\n   37:   (exact at every count, then trimmed at every count), so an exact cover at a\r\n   38:   HIGH count beat a trimmed cover at a LOW one. A 184-frame HuMo beat planned\r\n   39:   [85,33,33,33] because 184 is 0 mod 4 and an exact cover needs a count\r\n   40:   divisible by 4, while [153,33] trim 2 was legal at count 2 all along. One\r\n   41:   walk now. Differential over 798,510 (contract,target) pairs / 2,538 contract\r\n   42:   shapes: 46,949 plans changed, EVERY ONE a count reduction, zero refusals\r\n   43:   introduced, zero increases. Mutation 9/9, controls 5/5.\r\n   44:   **WIRE-W2 `a218b1f7`** -- DeferredImageGapError(RenderError) in the new leaf\r\n   45:   nodes/_otr_video_engines/render_errors.py; RenderError moved with it and is\r\n   46:   re-exported. Five cast-time sites declare themselves deferrable, three\r\n   47:   post-image and two wrong-aspect sites stay terminal, and BOTH fail-open\r\n   48:   swallows in ShotLock's cast-time preflight are deleted. Mutation 6/6.\r\n   49:   **WIRE-W6 `a14ecdfa`** -- the credits backdrop is the body video's frozen\r\n   50:   final frame; plan_backdrop DELETED (it read the clip manifest, which is why\r\n   51:   an all-mesh_stage episode rendered 7/7 and published nothing). Terminal vs\r\n   52:   presentation-only boundary per r4/A7. Mutation 4/4.\r\n   53: Found and NOT built (filed in OPEN BUGS): the fewest-segments rule can accept a\r\n   54:   disproportionate trim on a wide DISCRETE menu -- a bound was written,\r\n   55:   MEASURED (it made 4,885 grid cases worse) and REVERTED; unreachable on any\r\n   56:   shipped contract. And the B7 forbidden sweep only diffs TRACKED files, so a\r\n   57:   new test file passes its gate and fails the commit after -- that cost one red\r\n   58:   HEAD this session and is written down so it costs nobody else one.\r\n   59: The fan-out paid three times, all on my own new code: the WIRE-W1 property test\r\n   60:   compared segment COUNT only (a reversed ladder fill order passed it with 0\r\n   61:   mismatches over 27,954 plans), its floor was 500 against a real 27,954, and\r\n   62:   the trim bound above. All three fixed before the push.\r\n   63: Current step: WIRE-W3 (WAN) -- UNET-only hoist, VAE in the session identity,\r\n   64:   external_results injection, teardown dropping external refs before base\r\n   65:   release, native-frame-count + extension-mode receipts, and ping-pong\r\n   66:   suppressed for coverage-planned segments ONLY (it stays load-bearing for the\r\n   67:   shipped 8GB WAN tier).\r\n   68: Next: WIRE-W3 -> WIRE-W4 -> WIRE-W7 -> WIRE-W5, same window rules.\r\n   69: Models: Claude (rung 4) + a 3-lens Sonnet fan-out per chunk (rung 4, cheap) +\r\n   70:   one general-purpose read of the superseded GO_FORWARD region. No Codex spend\r\n   71:   -- no chunk needed a third attempt, so the two-strikes law never fired.\r\n   72: Commits: 5efd2baf, a218b1f7, a14ecdfa (+ this handoff).\r\n   73: \r\n   74: ## 2026-07-29 -- HEAD ead920d2 (v2.0-alpha) -- OPERATOR: LEAN-MEAN OFF GO_FORWARD\r\n   75: **Operator direction, same session as the plan repair below:** \"Lean-mean\r\n   76: should only come after the randomization and the SFX. In fact, maybe just put\r\n   77: lean-mean back onto the roadmap and not on the go-forward plan.\" Both halves\r\n   78: executed.\r\n   79: \r\n   80: **GO_FORWARD no longer carries lean-mean in any executable form.** Removed: the\r\n   81: two \"Big blocks\" entries (FRONT and TAIL) with renumbering; both lines from the\r\n   82: Coder queue fence; the CODER D and CODER G packing rows (struck through, gates\r\n   83: voided, \"do not re-add this row\" on each); the full `r2 -> r3 -> r4` operator\r\n   84: pin from the STANDING RE-GROUND GATE; items 5 and 6 of the live-order list;\r\n   85: CODER F's \"after D\" gate. The 07-24 rescue paragraph's order line was already\r\n   86: struck; it now reads \"IS NOT ON THIS PLAN AT ALL\". Every surviving mention in\r\n   87: the file is a pointer, a banner, or a struck historical line -- verified by\r\n   88: grep, 40 hits, none of them a queue position.\r\n   89: \r\n   90: **ROADMAP.md is now its only home, and it moved DOWN there too:** order 1 ->\r\n   91: order 3, behind SFX and product expansion, ahead of RunPod/install and the v2\r\n   92: release. That last part is deliberate and worth keeping: validating an install\r\n   93: path and tagging a release against a tree still full of dead code would have to\r\n   94: be redone after the rip. Section headings renumbered to match the table, and\r\n   95: GO_FORWARD's nine `ROADMAP.md section 1` cites were changed to a NAME-based\r\n   96: reference so the next renumber cannot break them.\r\n   97: \r\n   98: **NOTHING WAS LOST IN THE MOVE.** The new ROADMAP section carries the FRONT and\r\n   99: TAIL chunk chains, all six required edges, the full `r2 -> r3 -> r4` operator\r\n  100: pin with its reasoning, the panel composition and the Fable single-gate, the\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
