{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command \"if(Test-Path -LiteralPath 'kibitz-runs/2026-07-28-local-engine-obs-wiring/r3/final.md') { Get-Content -Raw -LiteralPath 'kibitz-runs/2026-07-28-local-engine-obs-wiring/r3/final.md' } else { 'MISSING' }\"","aggregated_output":"# r3 FINAL -- the wiring, judged. THIS IS THE BUILD SPEC.\n\nJudge: Claude/Opus (driver seat, anchor at `r3/anchor_opus.md`), HEAD\n`82844082`. Panel: codex `gpt-5.6-sol` high + agy `Gemini 3.6 Flash (High)`.\nOperator's call: the driver writes the Opus review directly rather than\nspawning a third seat.\n\n## W1 -- THE PARTITION FIX. Codex answered it exactly.\n\nMy anchor refused agy's mechanism (\"`_ladder_partition` returns None on\n`118 % 4`\") because the code I read TRUNCATES with `residue // q` and rejects\nonly on a bound. **I was right to refuse it, and codex supplied the real\nmechanism:** `coverage_plan.py:315-349` exhausts EXACT covers across ALL counts\nbefore trying trim candidates, which contradicts its own count-first contract.\n\nFIX: for each count, try exact first, then a permitted TRIMMED total, then\nadvance to the next count.\n\nPINNED EXPECTED VALUES, from codex, to go straight into\n`tests/test_multiclip_coverage_plan.py`:\n\n    target 184 -> [153, 33], trim_tail_frames=2   (TWO segments, not four)\n    targets 185..240 -> two segments under this policy\n\nAlso audit every existing trimmable multi-clip vector for intended count\nchanges -- this fix moves numbers that other tests may already assert.\n\n## W2 -- THE TYPED EXCEPTION. Both agy proposals were wrong.\n\n**agy's placement creates the cycle it was meant to avoid.**\n`render_driver.py:35` already imports `_otr_shared/retry_taxonomy.py`, and\n`RenderError` is defined at `render_driver.py:126-130`. Putting\n`DeferredImageGapError(RenderError)` in `retry_taxonomy` imports it back.\nFIX: move `RenderError` AND the subclass into a dependency-leaf module, then\nre-export both from `render_driver.py` so existing callers keep working.\n\n**agy's conversion sites were wrong and would have opened a hole.** The\ndeferred CAST-TIME gaps are `render_driver.py:1985, 2049, 2105, 2146, 2179`.\nDo NOT convert `:1024, :1055, :1084` -- those are POST-image validation and are\nTERMINAL; deferring there conceals a failed image-generation stage. Do NOT\nconvert `:1887, :2114` (wrong-style/aspect) either. CUT the proposed\n`content_oracle.py` / `role_slots.py` changes entirely.\n\nMy anchor worried that inheriting `RenderError` makes the broad handler and the\nnarrow handler the same catch. Codex resolves it without changing the base:\nin `otr_shot_lock.py:990-1013` catch ONLY `DeferredImageGapError` and re-raise\nevery other `RenderError`, `ValueError` and unexpected exception. The generic\nswallow at `:1011-1013` is today a FAIL-OPEN path and must go.\n\n## W3 -- WAN. The contract itself has to be narrowed.\n\n`BeatSession` today promises model + CLIP + VAE acquired once\n(`beat_session.py:1-32`), but W3 mandates UNET-only hoisting. So the DOCUMENTED\nAND TESTED contract narrows to: **\"primary diffusion patcher once per beat;\nauxiliaries may reload.\"** Ship that wording with the code or the next reader\nwill treat auxiliary reloads as a defect.\n\nImplement per WAN adapter: `session_identity()`, UNET-only `prepare()`,\n`external_results` graph injection, immediate ownership registration, teardown\nthat drops external references BEFORE base release (order per\n`eng_ltx_8gb.py:1297-1319`). Identity includes both UNET and CLIP loader\nmodes/receipts even though CLIP stays per-segment.\n\n**New blocker codex found:** `eng_wan_ti2v.py:698-733` may floor native\ngeneration and PING-PONG EXTEND it, while `coverage_plan.py:3-6` forbids\nloop/ping-pong coverage. Record native frame count and extension mode on every\nreceipt and have the grader reject ping-pong on lanes claiming real multi-clip.\nCompute the native budget AFTER prepared-model residency so every segment sees\nthe same memory state.\n\n## W4 -- HuMo. Two corrections that reorder the work.\n\n**HuMo needs the session work BEFORE the slicer.** `eng_humo.py` supplies\nneither identity nor prepared handles, so `beat_session.py:148-167` refuses it\nregardless of audio. Identity must pin recipe + UNET/LoRA/CLIP/VAE/audio-encoder\nreceipts and exclude prompt, seed, dimensions and per-segment audio.\n\n**Audio extraction is currently sequenced INSIDE the session.**\n`render_driver.py:3014-3020` enters `BeatSession` before invoking the request\nbuilder -- so ffmpeg would do filesystem work while holding the GPU lease and\nthe hoisted model. **Prebuild and validate all segment requests and audio\nslices BEFORE entering `BeatSession`;** only terminal-image chaining stays in\nthe render loop.\n\nField-name correction: the property is `CoverageSegment.visible_frames`\n(`coverage_plan.py:76-79`). `contributes` does not exist -- I used the wrong\nname in r2. Start from cumulative prior visible frames, duration from current\nvisible frames, on INTEGER SAMPLE boundaries, never accumulated float seconds.\n\nSource priority is already established and must be preserved: per-line voice\nWAV first, master audio only as fallback (`render_driver.py:1130-1148,\n2196-2262`). Receipt carries source PCM hash, segment index, start sample,\nsample count, rate/channels, output PCM hash. Durable audio goes under the\ncanonical episode directory, not temp. Thread the CONFIGURED ffmpeg through --\n`_slice_master_audio` hard-codes `ffmpeg` at `:410-462` while\n`otr_credits_roll.py:1170-1179` honours the project config.\n\nScope: HuMo/audio-driven-face multi-segment only. A generic all-engine slicer\nis CUT until chain-overlap and head-drop semantics are separately specified.\n\n## W5/W6 -- ORDER REVERSED, and the failure contract finally has a boundary\n\n**Build W6 BEFORE W5** -- acceptance cannot be written before the component\nthat defines OBS-complete output exists.\n\nThe grader reads the FROZEN route and delivered `engine_id` from the\nledger/manifest. It must NOT call `route_freeze.py:182-197` against the live\nenvironment: the director freezes at `otr_video_director.py:387-433` and\nShotLock validates at `otr_shot_lock.py:1521-1544`, so grading against later\nenvironment state is a clock-domain mismatch. agy's \"query the private\n`_NEVER_HUMO_REDIRECT_ENGINE` dynamically\" is CUT for the same reason.\n\n**The end card boundary** (this is what the Fable ruling needed to be\nbuildable): structural TRUTH failures stay terminal; PRESENTATION-ONLY failure\nmay return the already-completed body with a declared zero-length credits tail\nand a warning receipt. Without that split, \"constitutionally incapable of\nfailing\" and the existing no-fallback credits contract cannot both hold.\n\n**End-card source, simpler than my anchor said:** do NOT read the raw final\nmanifest clip. `otr_silent_composite.py:806-825` has ALREADY flattened\ndirectory clips into the assembled body video, so the reliable source is the\nfinal frame of CreditsRoll's incoming `video_path`. Extract, freeze, dim,\noverlay. CreditsRoll never learns what a directory clip is. CUT raw\ndirectory-clip support inside CreditsRoll.\n\n## THE GAP NOBODY OWNED -- codex MUST-FIX 11\n\n**No W1-W6 step enforces the operator's three rulings.** Nothing makes every\naudio-in beat receive a mouth-bearing still, nothing makes the radio-face the\ndefault, nothing enforces one overheard human face per episode. The plan has\nthe rulings and no owner for them.\n\nAdd an explicit owner (verify in `otr_meta_brief_image_prompt.py`,\n`otr_image_director.py`, `otr_image_gen_dispatcher.py`) plus LEDGER-LEVEL\nCARDINALITY CHECKS before build. This is now W7 and it is not optional -- it is\nthe operator's ruling, and an unowned ruling is a ruling that silently lapses.\n\n## BUILD ORDER (final)\n\n    W1 partition fix        -- pinned values above; resizes everything downstream\n    W2 typed exception      -- leaf module, 5 sites, narrow catch, kill the swallow\n    W6 end card             -- cheapest, DELETES a failure mode\n    W3 WAN session          -- UNET-only, narrowed contract, ping-pong receipt\n    W4 HuMo session + audio -- session FIRST, slices prebuilt OUTSIDE BeatSession\n    W7 mouth-still ownership-- enforce the three rulings, ledger cardinality\n    W5 acceptance grader    -- reads the FROZEN route, last\n\nEvery chunk: full suite + Bug Bible, `OTR_WorkflowValidator` on\n`workflows/otr_canonical.json` with JSON round-trip and link/widget audit,\nbyte-identical unless a node contract genuinely changes. Commit AND push green.\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_43","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command \"if(Test-Path -LiteralPath 'kibitz-runs/2026-07-28-local-engine-obs-wiring/r4/final.md') { Get-Content -Raw -LiteralPath 'kibitz-runs/2026-07-28-local-engine-obs-wiring/r4/final.md' } else { 'MISSING' }\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_43","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command \"if(Test-Path -LiteralPath 'kibitz-runs/2026-07-28-local-engine-obs-wiring/r4/final.md') { Get-Content -Raw -LiteralPath 'kibitz-runs/2026-07-28-local-engine-obs-wiring/r4/final.md' } else { 'MISSING' }\"","aggregated_output":"# r4 FINAL -- convergence. Build from r3/final.md AS AMENDED BELOW.\n\nJudge: Claude/Opus (driver), HEAD `82844082`. Panel: codex `gpt-5.6-sol` high\n+ agy `Gemini 3.6 Flash (High)`. agy: \"yes-with-fixes\". codex: \"no\" with eight\nmust-fixes, and it is right on all eight. Amendments are small and specific;\nthe ARC IS CONVERGED and the build order stands.\n\n## A1 -- I REGRESSED THE OPERATOR'S RULING IN MY OWN r3 SUMMARY. Fix first.\n\nr3/final.md says \"one overheard human face per episode\". The ruling\n(`GO_FORWARD_PLAN.md:77-104`) is **ZERO OR ONE**, and only for an explicitly\nqualified private/confession/final line whose coverage fits ONE SEGMENT.\nMy wording implies exactly one and drops the eligibility rule and the\ntuning-eye QC requirements. Restore in full:\n\n    radio mouth BY DEFAULT; zero or one human face, only for a qualified\n    private/confession/final line with single-segment coverage; otherwise zero.\n    Enforce the late-1930s tuning eye, no legible text, no sharp slats or\n    focused straight edges, static wood, and REGENERATE on violation.\n\nCUT (codex): do not make Python infer \"private\" or \"confession\" from prose.\nUse an explicit durable semantic field, or choose the radio. If no such field\nexists, select ZERO human faces. That is the safe default and it needs no new\nheuristic subsystem.\n\n## A2 -- W7 needed a seam, not a list of three files. Codex supplied it.\n\n\"Add an owner (verify in three files)\" was not implementable:\n`otr_meta_brief_image_prompt.py` runs BEFORE ShotLock knows `segment_count`,\nbut single-take eligibility is decided by the coverage plan IN ShotLock.\nThe seam:\n\n    ImageDirector      freezes the audio-in/talking recipe\n    MetaBrief          authors radio + eligible-human CANDIDATES\n    ShotLock           SOLE per-beat selection + cardinality owner, after\n                       effective routing and coverage are known\n    ImageGenDispatcher materializes the selected object\n    render_driver      consumes the selected object\n\nLedger validation: exactly ONE mouth-bearing still per `audio_ref` shot, human\ncount <= 1.\n\n## A3 -- THE HUMO BLOCKER. This would have silently broken W4.\n\n`eng_humo.py:525-531` calls `_wb.reclaim_idle_models()` AFTER EVERY SEGMENT.\nLeaving that active evicts the handles we just hoisted, between segments --\nthe session would look correct and reload the model anyway. Suppress\nper-segment reclaim inside `BeatSession`; reclaim ONCE at teardown, after\ndropping `external_results` and graph references.\n**Test real loader/model invocation counts and VRAM residency, NOT `prepare()`\ncall counts** -- call counts would show green while the model reloaded.\n\n## A4 -- the audio length contract was wrong in r3, and this is the fix\n\nr3 said feed `visible_frames` of audio. But the graph's generation length stays\n`render_frames` (`eng_humo.py:472-484`): for the pinned 184 case that is 31\naudio frames against a 33-frame render.\nCONTRACT: conditioning WAV duration EQUALS `render_frames`; copy only the\n`visible_frames` source interval and APPEND SILENCE for `trim_tail_frames` --\nnever speech from the next segment. Ledger contribution and sample accounting\nstay at `visible_frames`.\nFLAGGED AS AN ASSUMPTION by codex: verify the installed `WanHuMoImageToVideo`\nshort-audio behaviour before locking this. First build step of W4.\n\n## A5 -- WAN identity omits the VAE, and for TI2V that is material\n\nBoth adapters load a VAE independently (`eng_wan_i2v.py:399-460`,\n`eng_wan_ti2v.py:591-647`), and TI2V explicitly distinguishes INCOMPATIBLE VAE\ngenerations (`eng_wan_ti2v.py:16-19,79-84`). Add the resolved VAE token/path\nreceipt to the immutable session recipe.\n\nSame class for HuMo (codex MF-4): loader names, dimensions, steps, CFG and the\nnegative prompt are re-read from env (`eng_humo.py:270-278,319-359`). Resolve\nONE immutable beat-session configuration BEFORE loading, and use it for\nidentity, `prepare()` and every segment graph. Exclude only per-segment prompt,\nseed, frame count and sliced audio.\n\n## A6 -- the grader, made concrete\n\nName a durable repository script. Per shot require\n`video.shots[].engine_id == video.roles_effective[shot.role]`, then require\nevery delivered clip-manifest row's `engine_id` to match that frozen expected\nvalue (manifest carries delivered IDs at `render_driver.py:4030-4099`).\nCUT aggregate engine histograms as acceptance evidence -- they cannot detect\ntwo shots EXCHANGING engines while totals stay identical. Grade OBS publication\nand canonical artifacts separately. Never query live routing state.\n\n## A7 -- the end-card boundary, enumerated\n\nTERMINAL: missing/unreadable body video, malformed required ledger/manifest\ntruth, inability to return an existing body.\nPRESENTATION-ONLY (return the original body, `credits_tail_s=0`, structured\nwarning): terminal-frame extraction, dim/overlay, credits composition, credits\nencoding. Pin both branches around `otr_credits_roll.py:1331-1341`.\n\n## SUITE RISK -- answered\n\ncodex found NO existing count assertion that this fix alters: the pinned\nthree/four-segment cases use different capacity or `allow_tail_trim=False`.\nRe-verify after implementation. Add the 184 and 185-240 vectors to\n`tests/test_multiclip_coverage_plan.py`.\n\n## BUILD ORDER -- UNCHANGED\n\n    W1 partition -> W2 typed exception -> W6 end card -> W3 WAN ->\n    W4 HuMo -> W7 mouth-still ownership -> W5 grader\n\ncodex's VERIFY-AT-BUILD checklist (r4/codex.md, final section) is adopted\nwholesale as the per-chunk gate. It is the best artifact this arc produced:\nfifteen checks, each one a receipt someone can hold up.\n\n## ARC CONVERGED\n\nFour rounds. The panel corrected me in every single one -- the taxonomy in r1,\nthe scope estimate in r2, the exception sites and the ordering in r3, and my\nown paraphrase of the operator's ruling in r4. Nothing here is a design\nquestion any more. Go and build it.\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
