{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_51","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command '$n=0; Get-Content -LiteralPath '\"'docs/PROD_BUG_LOG.md' | ForEach-Object { \"'$n++; if($n -ge 1 -and $n -le 140) { '\"'{0,5}: {1}' -f \"'$n,$_ } }'","aggregated_output":"    1: # Production Bug Log (staging pre-Bible)\r\n    2: \r\n    3: **Contract (operator, 2026-07-10):** Claude appends entries here AUTONOMOUSLY, but\r\n    4: ONLY for bugs that actually failed in a live/prod run (live render, headless lane,\r\n    5: soak, published episode). Dev/audit/review catches get fixed, never logged. NO entry\r\n    6: here touches the Bug Bible directly -- at ship time the operator triggers a BUG\r\n    7: FAN-OUT over this log, which promotes approved entries into the survival-guide\r\n    8: Bible in bulk under the Three-File Contract (YAML + README count + regression\r\n    9: test, one commit). Promoted entries get a `- promotion: BUG-...` mapping;\r\n   10: rejected ones get marked `REJECTED` and stay for the record. Append-only,\r\n   11: newest last.\r\n   12: \r\n   13: `promotion` and `status` are deliberately separate axes. `promotion` means a\r\n   14: real production incident has supplied a reusable Bible rule; `status` continues\r\n   15: to describe the implementation's own fix/requalification state. A fixed rule\r\n   16: may therefore be promoted while its same-seed 120-word confirmation remains in\r\n   17: progress. Conversely, an unproven review finding never receives either marker.\r\n   18: Running tests/bug_bible_regression.py after every code change stays automatic\r\n   19: and is unrelated to this log.\r\n   20: \r\n   21: Entry format:\r\n   22: \r\n   23: ```\r\n   24: ## PBUG-YYYYMMDD-NN -- short title\r\n   25: - surfaced: <which live run: smoke/soak/episode + date>\r\n   26: - symptom: <one line, what the operator/log saw>\r\n   27: - root cause: <one line>\r\n   28: - fix: <commit sha + one line>\r\n   29: - verify idea: <candidate machine check for the future bible test>\r\n   30: - bible-worthy: <yes/no guess + why -- operator decides at fan-out>\r\n   31: - promotion: <BUG-id after approved fan-out; omit while pending>\r\n   32: - status: OPEN | PROMOTED <id> | REJECTED\r\n   33: ```\r\n   34: \r\n   35: ---\r\n   36: \r\n   37: Backfill note: entries PBUG-20260612-01 .. PBUG-20260711-02 were mined 2026-07-10/11\r\n   38: by a two-agent backsweep (git history + handoff/smoke docs), prod-only bar applied,\r\n   39: cross-checked against BUG_BIBLE.yaml (BUG-11.26 family, 12.47, 07.16 excluded as\r\n   40: already promoted). Confidence tags preserved from the sweep.\r\n   41: \r\n   42: ## PBUG-20260612-01 -- headless boot dies on cp1252 emoji print\r\n   43: - surfaced: detached headless soak/API boot, 2026-06-12\r\n   44: - symptom: boot dies ~13s, exit 1, \"SERVER DID NOT COME UP\"\r\n   45: - root cause: detached cmd inherits cp1252; prestartup_script.py printed U+2705/U+2713 -> UnicodeEncodeError\r\n   46: - fix: scripts/_otr_soak_server_launch.cmd sets PYTHONUTF8=1 + PYTHONIOENCODING=utf-8; rule codified in CLAUDE.md section 5\r\n   47: - verify idea: launcher-path boot succeeds; any new boot path asserts UTF-8 env\r\n   48: - bible-worthy: yes -- Windows console-codec boot killer, hits any custom node that prints unicode at import\r\n   49: - confidence: MED (sourced from operating-rules doc, no dated incident log)\r\n   50: - status: PROMOTED BUG-02.15\r\n   51: \r\n   52: ## PBUG-20260616-01 -- LTX-AV soak VRAM peak 15.8GB over the 14.5GB cap\r\n   53: - surfaced: LTX full-episode soak, 2026-06-16 (976ab329)\r\n   54: - symptom: soak measured 15.8GB peak on a 14.5GB gate, both device modes\r\n   55: - root cause: Gemma text encoder stayed GPU-resident through the LTX pass\r\n   56: - fix: b0925c37 moved encoder to cpu; 1e5d66f4 REVERTED it after soak re-measure proved the offload ineffective -- record documents a fix att